§ `Cases -- Dangerous materials and devices: explosives, sections 79 to 82.1 (lines 1189-1218)`
#ASSERT `Under section 79, am I under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by an explosive substance` TRUE `anything intended to be used to make an explosive substance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 79, am I under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by an explosive substance` FALSE `anything intended to be used to make an explosive substance` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 79, am I under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by an explosive substance` TRUE `a thing that is none of those` EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 2 "includes": the thing is left open
#ASSERT `Under section 80, have I committed the offence of breach of the duty of care with an explosive substance` TRUE `anything intended to be used to make an explosive substance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 80, have I committed the offence of breach of the duty of care with an explosive substance` TRUE `anything intended to be used to make an explosive substance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- with lawful excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 80, what class of offence is breach of the duty of care with an explosive substance` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `Under section 80, what is the most imprisonment I face for breach of the duty of care, given what happened as a result` `s 80(a) an explosion occurs as a result that causes death or is likely to cause death to any person` EQUALS JUST `imprisonment for life`   -- an explosion that causes or is likely to cause death
#ASSERT `Under section 80, what is the most imprisonment I face for breach of the duty of care, given what happened as a result` `s 80(b) an explosion occurs as a result that causes bodily harm or damage to property or is likely to cause bodily harm or damage to property` EQUALS JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)   -- bodily harm or damage to property
#ASSERT `Under section 80, what is the most imprisonment I face for breach of the duty of care, given what happened as a result` `s 80 no explosion occurs as a result` EQUALS NOTHING   -- no explosion: the section states no penalty
