#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(1), may a provincial court judge order that the documents I receive be edited to remove identifying information` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the judge does not consider it necessary

-- Under section 110.3(1), what does an order to delete identifying information direct
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(1), what does an order to delete identifying information direct` EQUALS (LIST `s 110.3(1) that copies be made of any documents relating to the order made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1), including the order itself`, `s 110.3(1) that any information that could identify the person who applied for the order, or anyone known to the person, be deleted from those copies`, `s 110.3(1) that the documents to which the public has access or that are made available to or required to be served on any person are to be the edited copies`)   -- (a) copies, (b) identifying information deleted from them, (c) the edited copies are what the public may see and what is served

-- Under section 110.3(2), may the order to delete identifying information be for any period, definite or indefinite
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(2), may the order to delete identifying information be for any period, definite or indefinite` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the judge considers the period necessary to protect the security of the applicant   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 110.3(2), may the order to delete identifying information be for an indefinite period` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; question retitled in the second seat audit to what the layer-1 function answers, answer unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(2), may the order to delete identifying information be for any period, definite or indefinite` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the judge does not   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 110.3(2), may the order to delete identifying information be for an indefinite period` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; question retitled in the second seat audit to what the layer-1 function answers, answer unchanged

-- Under section 110.3(3), must the originals of the documents be sealed
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(3), must the originals of the documents be sealed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an order is made under subsection 110.3(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(3), must the originals of the documents be sealed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no order is made: an "if" that fails

-- Under section 110.3(4), may an application to revoke or vary the order to delete identifying information be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(4), may an application to revoke or vary the order to delete identifying information be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an order was made and I apply to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 110.3(4), may I apply to revoke or vary the order to delete identifying information` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; question retitled in the second seat audit to what the layer-1 function answers, answer unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(4), may an application to revoke or vary the order to delete identifying information be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an order was made but I apply elsewhere   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 110.3(4), may I apply to revoke or vary the order to delete identifying information` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; question retitled in the second seat audit to what the layer-1 function answers, answer unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(4), may an application to revoke or vary the order to delete identifying information be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no order was made   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 110.3(4), may I apply to revoke or vary the order to delete identifying information` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; question retitled in the second seat audit to what the layer-1 function answers, answer unchanged

-- Under section 110.3(5), does an order to delete identifying information still apply to the hearing of the application against me
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(5), does an order to delete identifying information still apply to the hearing of the application against me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a date is fixed for the hearing and the order is still in force
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(5), does an order to delete identifying information still apply to the hearing of the application against me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a date is fixed but the order is no longer in force
#ASSERT `Under section 110.3(5), does an order to delete identifying information still apply to the hearing of the application against me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no date is fixed

