#ASSERT `Under section 110.4(3), may the provincial court judge adjourn the hearing on my application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 110.4(3), may the provincial court judge adjourn the hearing on my application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is of the where, when or upon kind, so the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (test 3(i)) lists the function and leaves the answer as the guide's ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 gives it: JUST FALSE, not NOTHING (an element is missing: the application is made before or at any time during the hearing)

