#ASSERT (`Under section 117.01(3)(a), what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment for an offence under section 117.01`)'s `maximum imprisonment` EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
#ASSERT (`Under section 117.01(3)(a), what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment for an offence under section 117.01`)'s `mode` EQUALS `by indictment`

§§ `s 117.0101 Application for emergency limitations on access order`

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(1), may a person make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an emergency order limiting access to things in my possession` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(1), may a person make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an emergency order limiting access to things in my possession` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the person against whom the order is sought cohabits with, or is an associate of, another person who is prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(1), may a person make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an emergency order limiting access to things in my possession` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the other person would or might have access to any such thing that is in the possession of the person against whom the order is sought

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(2), may the provincial court judge hold the hearing of the application in private` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(2), may the provincial court judge hold the hearing of the application in private` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(3), is the provincial court judge bound to make an emergency order limiting my use and possession of firearms and similar things` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(3), is the provincial court judge bound to make an emergency order limiting my use and possession of firearms and similar things` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an element is missing: the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) has concluded
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(3), is the provincial court judge bound to make an emergency order limiting my use and possession of firearms and similar things` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an element is missing: the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(3), is the provincial court judge bound to make an emergency order limiting my use and possession of firearms and similar things` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an element is missing: the judge is satisfied that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person


#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(3), is the period of the emergency order I face not more than 30 days` 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(3), is the period of the emergency order I face not more than 30 days` 31 EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(4), is a copy of the emergency order to be served on me` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(4), is a copy of the emergency order to be served on me` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: an order has been made under subsection (3)

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(5), is the provincial court judge bound to impose the least intrusive terms and conditions possible in my emergency order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(5), is the provincial court judge bound to impose the least intrusive terms and conditions possible in my emergency order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the judge determines terms and conditions under subsection (3)

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(10), may the judge issue a warrant, or include a requirement to surrender, in my emergency order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(10), may the judge issue a warrant, or include a requirement to surrender, in my emergency order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an element is missing: the judge is satisfied that there is no other way to ensure that the terms and conditions of that order can reasonably be complied with

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(6), may the provincial court judge issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search for and seize things in my possession` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(6), may the provincial court judge issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search for and seize things in my possession` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3) possesses, in a building, receptacle or place, a thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(6), may the provincial court judge issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search for and seize things in my possession` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the judge is satisfied that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess the thing

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(7), may a peace officer search for and seize things in my possession without a warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(7), may a peace officer search for and seize things in my possession without a warrant` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: s 2 peace officer: the officer is one
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(7), may a peace officer search for and seize things in my possession without a warrant` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the person is subject to an order made under subsection (3)
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(7), may a peace officer search for and seize things in my possession without a warrant` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, for the person to possess a thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(7), may a peace officer search for and seize things in my possession without a warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (6) exist
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(7), may a peace officer search for and seize things in my possession without a warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(8), is the peace officer who searched or seized bound to make a report immediately to a justice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(8), is the peace officer who searched or seized bound to make a report immediately to a justice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the peace officer executes a warrant referred to in subsection (6) / the peace officer conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (7)

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(8), does the peace officer's report show what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(8), does the peace officer's report show what the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the report is of an execution of a warrant and shows the things, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant / the report is of a search without a warrant and shows the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things, if any, seized

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(9), may the provincial court judge require me to surrender things to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(9), may the provincial court judge require me to surrender things to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the judge makes an order against the person under subsection (3)
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(9), may the provincial court judge require me to surrender things to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the judge is satisfied by information on oath that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of any person for the person to possess the thing
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(9), may the provincial court judge require me to surrender things to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the thing is in the person's possession on the day on which the order is made and its use or possession is subject to terms and conditions under the order

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(9), is the judge bound to specify a reasonable period for me to surrender the thing` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(9), is the judge bound to specify a reasonable period for me to surrender the thing` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an element is missing: the judge requires the person to surrender the thing

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(11), may the officer return to me the thing seized or surrendered before the emergency order expires or is revoked` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(11), may the officer return to me the thing seized or surrendered before the emergency order expires or is revoked` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the thing has been seized under subsection (6) or (7) by the peace officer / the thing has been surrendered in accordance with subsection (9) to the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(11), may the officer return to me the thing seized or surrendered before the emergency order expires or is revoked` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person will comply with the terms and conditions of the order as to the use and possession of the thing
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(11), may the officer return to me the thing seized or surrendered before the emergency order expires or is revoked` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(11), may the officer return to me the thing seized or surrendered before the emergency order expires or is revoked` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is of the where, when or upon kind, so the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (test 3(i)) lists the function and leaves the answer as the guide's ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 gives it: JUST FALSE, not NOTHING; the two where-kind limbs ("before the expiry or revocation", "on being issued a receipt") now answer JUST FALSE, and the "if the officer has reasonable grounds" limb stays NOTHING (the exception applies: a receipt for it is issued)
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(11), may the officer return to me the thing seized or surrendered before the emergency order expires or is revoked` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(11), may the officer return to me the thing seized or surrendered before the emergency order expires or is revoked` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is of the where, when or upon kind, so the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (test 3(i)) lists the function and leaves the answer as the guide's ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 gives it: JUST FALSE, not NOTHING; the two where-kind limbs ("before the expiry or revocation", "on being issued a receipt") now answer JUST FALSE, and the "if the officer has reasonable grounds" limb stays NOTHING (the exception applies: the order has not expired or been revoked)

#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(12), are the things seized or surrendered to be returned to me after the emergency order is revoked or its period ends` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person states every element
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(12), are the things seized or surrendered to be returned to me after the emergency order is revoked or its period ends` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the things were seized under subsection (6) or (7) from a person against whom an order has been made under subsection (3), or surrendered by the person in accordance with subsection (9)
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(12), are the things seized or surrendered to be returned to me after the emergency order is revoked or its period ends` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked / the period specified in the order made against the person under subsection (3) has ended
#ASSERT `Under section 117.0101(12), are the things seized or surrendered to be returned to me after the emergency order is revoked or its period ends` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the exception applies: the things have already been returned under subsection (11)

