#ASSERT `Under section 145(9), is the certificate evidence of its statements without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: the certificate is that of the clerk of the court or a judge of the court before which the accused is alleged to have failed to attend, or of the person in charge of the place at which it is alleged the accused failed to attend for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act
#ASSERT `Under section 145(9), is the certificate evidence of its statements without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an element is missing: in proceedings under subsection (2), the certificate states that the accused failed to attend court as required by the release order or, having attended court, failed to subsequently attend court as required, or failed to surrender in accordance with an order / in proceedings under subsection (3), the certificate states that the accused was named in an appearance notice confirmed by a justice under section 508 and failed to attend court in accordance with the notice or failed to appear at the time and place stated in it / in proceedings under subsection (3), the certificate states that a summons was issued to and served on the accused and the accused failed to attend court in accordance with it or failed to appear at the time and place stated in it / in proceedings under subsection (4), the certificate states that the accused was at large on an undertaking confirmed by a justice under section 508 and failed to attend court in accordance with it or failed to appear at the time and place stated in it

