-- ccc7-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for the seat layer ccc7-seat.l4: Criminal Code (Canada), Part VI, sections 183 to 196.1, asked by the person who is, or may be, accused.
-- GENERATED from work/cases_def.py by work/gen_cases.py (the generator is not shipped); the file is plain L4 and is read and run as it stands.
-- Each case is one #ASSERT of a seat question over plain facts, with the expected answer written by hand from the text beside it. A comment states the facts the person gives; every other fact is the plain "no" (FALSE, 0, "").
-- Every one of the questions is asked at least once, and every answer kind is asserted where the question has it: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, and NOTHING (not covered: a case outside the encoding).
-- Dates are worked by hand; sixty days counted inclusively, so 1 January to 1 March 2025 is sixty days (31 + 28 + 1).

