§ `Section 183.1 -- Consent of one of several people`
-- A conference call: made by several people, one of them agreed to the recording (stated: the communication was made by more than one person or meant for more t; one of those persons consented to the interception)
#ASSERT `Under section 183.1, does this section make the consent of one person on the communication sufficient consent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A one-to-one call: the section speaks only of a communication made by, or meant for, several persons (stated: one of those persons consented to the interception)
#ASSERT `Under section 183.1, does this section make the consent of one person on the communication sufficient consent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A conference call, nobody agreed: the section says one person's consent is sufficient, and is silent on what follows when no one consented (stated: the communication was made by more than one person or meant for more t)
#ASSERT `Under section 183.1, does this section make the consent of one person on the communication sufficient consent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

