§ `Section 184.1 -- Interception to prevent bodily harm (situation: an agent of the state recorded a communication with one party's consent)`
-- A peace officer recorded a call with the caller's consent to prevent bodily harm to the caller (stated: the person is a peace officer; the interception was by a device, as section 183 defines it; it was a private communication, as section 183 defines it; one party to the communication consented to the interception; the agent believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodil; the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm)
#ASSERT `Under section 184.1(1), may an agent of the state intercept a private communication to prevent bodily harm` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A person acting in cooperation with a peace officer did the same (stated: the person is a peace officer; the interception was by a device, as section 183 defines it; it was a private communication, as section 183 defines it; one party to the communication consented to the interception; the agent believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodil; the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm; the person is acting under the authority of, or in cooperation with, a)
#ASSERT `Under section 184.1(1), may an agent of the state intercept a private communication to prevent bodily harm` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No reasonable grounds to believe there was a risk of bodily harm (stated: the person is a peace officer; the interception was by a device, as section 183 defines it; it was a private communication, as section 183 defines it; one party to the communication consented to the interception; the agent believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodil; the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm)
#ASSERT `Under section 184.1(1), may an agent of the state intercept a private communication to prevent bodily harm` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The person is neither a peace officer nor acting for one (stated: the person is a peace officer; the interception was by a device, as section 183 defines it; it was a private communication, as section 183 defines it; one party to the communication consented to the interception; the agent believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodil; the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm)
#ASSERT `Under section 184.1(1), may an agent of the state intercept a private communication to prevent bodily harm` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- What was recorded under 184.1(1), offered at a trial for fraud (no bodily harm alleged) (stated: it was obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection 184.1(1))
#ASSERT `Under section 184.1(2), are the contents of a private communication obtained from an interception under subsection 184.1(1) inadmissible as evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same, offered at a trial in which bodily harm is alleged (stated: it was obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection 184.1(1); the proceedings are ones in which bodily harm is alleged)
#ASSERT `Under section 184.1(2), are the contents of a private communication obtained from an interception under subsection 184.1(1) inadmissible as evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A recording not made under 184.1(1): not covered by this subsection
#ASSERT `Under section 184.1(2), are the contents of a private communication obtained from an interception under subsection 184.1(1) inadmissible as evidence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

