-- 199(2): a peace officer may, whether or not he is acting under a warrant, take into custody any person he finds keeping a common gaming house
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2), may a peace officer take me into custody without a warrant` (`a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace or for the service or execution of civil process`) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a peace officer: section 2's answer is NOTHING or no, and the section says what a peace officer may do, not what anyone else may
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2), may a peace officer take me into custody without a warrant` `the pilot in command of such an aircraft while it is not in flight` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the officer found you neither keeping nor in the house: not covered
