§ `Pari-mutuel betting (section 204)`

-- 204(1)(b): sections 201 and 202 do not apply to a private bet between individuals not engaged in any way in the business of betting
#ASSERT `Under section 204(1), do sections 201 and 202 not apply to a private bet between me and another individual` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- individuals engaged in the business of betting: the text says only what is exempt, not what else is not
#ASSERT `Under section 204(1), do sections 201 and 202 not apply to a private bet between me and another individual` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 204(3): no person or association shall use a pari-mutuel system in respect of a horse-race unless the system has been approved and is supervised
#ASSERT `Under section 204(3), am I prohibited from using a pari-mutuel system of betting on a horse-race` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- approved and supervised: the "unless" is met, so the prohibition does not apply
#ASSERT `Under section 204(3), am I prohibited from using a pari-mutuel system of betting on a horse-race` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 204(5): a custodian shall not deduct or retain any amount except as subsection (6) permits
#ASSERT `Under section 204(5), am I prohibited from deducting or retaining an amount from the money bet under a pari-mutuel system` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- made under subsection (6): the prohibition does not apply
#ASSERT `Under section 204(5), am I prohibited from deducting or retaining an amount from the money bet under a pari-mutuel system` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 204(10): every person who contravenes or fails to comply with a provision of this section or of the regulations is guilty of the offence
#ASSERT `Under section 204(10), have I committed the offence of contravening section 204 or its regulations` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- you did neither: the text does not say you are innocent, only who is guilty
#ASSERT `Under section 204(10), have I committed the offence of contravening section 204 or its regulations` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 204(10): guilty of (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years, or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction
#ASSERT `Under section 204(10), how serious is the offence of contravening section 204 or its regulations, and what can it cost me` EQUALS `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty` OF `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`, (LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)), TRUE

