§ `Duties tending to preservation of life (sections 214 to 218)`

-- 215(1)(a): a parent is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life for a child under the age of sixteen years
#ASSERT `Under section 215(1), am I under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life` TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the child is sixteen: not "under the age of sixteen years", the limit is the text's own wording, so not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 215(1), am I under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life` TRUE 16 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 215(1)(b): to provide necessaries of life to their spouse
#ASSERT `Under section 215(1), am I under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a common-law partner (cohabiting in a conjugal relationship for at least twelve months): 215(1)(b)
#ASSERT `Under section 215(1), am I under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life` FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE 12 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- eleven months is less than one year, so not a common-law partner (s 2), and no other limb applies
#ASSERT `Under section 215(1), am I under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life` FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE 11 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- a parent of a five-year-old who fails, without lawful excuse, to provide necessaries when the child is in necessitous circumstances: 215(2)(a)(i)
#ASSERT `Under section 215(2), have I committed the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the failure is without lawful excuse but the child is not destitute and no endangerment: "if (i) ... necessitous circumstances or (ii) the failure endangers life": an "if" that fails
#ASSERT `Under section 215(2), have I committed the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a lawful excuse: "fails without lawful excuse" is part of the offence's own wording ("Every person commits an offence who ..."), so an unmet element answers NOTHING (marginal reading M1); only the "if (i) ... or (ii) ..." conditions answer JUST FALSE (first draft of this expectation said JUST FALSE, which misapplied M1; corrected before the assertion was run again)
#ASSERT `Under section 215(2), have I committed the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no legal duty under 215(1) is shown: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 215(2), have I committed the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 215(2)(b): a person under your charge who cannot withdraw from it or provide for themselves, and the failure endangers their life or health: 215(2)(b)
#ASSERT `Under section 215(2), have I committed the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- 215(3): guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years, or an offence punishable on summary conviction
#ASSERT `Under section 215(3), how serious is the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life, and what can it cost me` EQUALS `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty` OF `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`, (LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)), TRUE

