-- 221: every person who by criminal negligence causes bodily harm to another person is guilty (bodily harm: a hurt or injury that interferes with health or comfort and is more than transient or trifling)
#ASSERT `Under section 221, have I committed the offence of causing bodily harm by criminal negligence` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the hurt was only transient or trifling: not bodily harm, so not covered by this section
#ASSERT `Under section 221, have I committed the offence of causing bodily harm by criminal negligence` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the harm was not caused by the negligence
#ASSERT `Under section 221, have I committed the offence of causing bodily harm by criminal negligence` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

