-- culpable homicide: section 222(4) and sections 229 to 240 say what offence; this subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 222(3), is my homicide an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 223(2): a person commits homicide when he causes injury to a child before or during its birth as a result of which the child dies after becoming a human being (one that has completely proceeded from the mother in a living state)
#ASSERT `Under section 223(2), have I committed homicide by injuring a child before or during its birth` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not in a living state: not a human being, so not homicide by this subsection (the text's own "when")
#ASSERT `Under section 223(2), have I committed homicide by injuring a child before or during its birth` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no injury caused by you
#ASSERT `Under section 223(2), have I committed homicide by injuring a child before or during its birth` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 224: where a person, by an act or omission, does anything that results in the death of a human being, he causes the death of that human being notwithstanding that death from that cause might have been prevented by resorting to proper means
#ASSERT `Under section 224, am I treated as having caused a death that my act or omission resulted in even if other causes contributed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a thing that resulted in death: the "where" is not met
#ASSERT `Under section 224, am I treated as having caused a death that my act or omission resulted in even if other causes contributed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 225: where a person causes to a human being a bodily injury that is of itself of a dangerous nature and from which death results, he causes the death of that human being notwithstanding that the immediate cause of death is proper or improper treatment
#ASSERT `Under section 225, am I treated as having caused a death that followed a dangerous bodily injury I caused` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- death did not result from the injury
#ASSERT `Under section 225, am I treated as having caused a death that followed a dangerous bodily injury I caused` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 226: where a person causes to a human being a bodily injury that results in death, he causes the death of that human being although the effect of the bodily injury is only to accelerate his death from a disease or disorder arising from some other cause
#ASSERT `Under section 226, am I treated as having caused a death that followed a bodily injury I caused` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no injury that resulted in death
#ASSERT `Under section 226, am I treated as having caused a death that followed a bodily injury I caused` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 227(1): no medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits culpable homicide if they provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2
#ASSERT `Under section 227(1), have I committed culpable homicide by providing medical assistance in dying` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
