§ `Medical assistance in dying (sections 241.1 to 241.4)`

-- 241.1: medical assistance in dying means the administering by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner of a substance to a person, at their request, that causes their death
#ASSERT `Under section 241.1, is what I did medical assistance in dying` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the two ways: "means"
#ASSERT `Under section 241.1, is what I did medical assistance in dying` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner: the definition is "means ... by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner"
#ASSERT `Under section 241.1, is what I did medical assistance in dying` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 241.2(1): a person may receive MAID only if eligible for health services, at least 18, capable, with a grievous and irremediable medical condition (serious and incurable illness, advanced irreversible decline, intolerable suffering), a voluntary request and informed consent
#ASSERT `Under section 241.2(1), does the person who has asked me for medical assistance in dying meet all of the criteria` TRUE 40 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- seventeen is under eighteen: a criterion is not met ("only if")
#ASSERT `Under section 241.2(1), does the person who has asked me for medical assistance in dying meet all of the criteria` TRUE 17 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the only illness relied on is a mental illness: it is not considered an illness, disease or disability, so there is no grievous and irremediable medical condition
#ASSERT `Under section 241.2(1), does the person who has asked me for medical assistance in dying meet all of the criteria` TRUE 40 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 241.2(1): a person may receive medical assistance in dying only if they meet all of the criteria
#ASSERT `Under section 241.2(1), may the person receive medical assistance in dying` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "only if" states a necessary condition, not a sufficient one: meeting the criteria does not itself say the person may receive it
#ASSERT `Under section 241.2(1), may the person receive medical assistance in dying` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 241.2(3): before a practitioner provides MAID the practitioner must be of the opinion that the person meets the criteria, and the request, witness, withdrawal information, second opinion, independence and final consent requirements must be met (here no difficulty communicating, so paragraph (g) is not engaged)
