§ `Impeding rescue, and the duty to guard openings and excavations (sections 262 and 263)`

-- 262(a): prevents or impedes any person who is attempting to save his own life
#ASSERT `Under section 262, have I committed the offence of impeding an attempt to save a life` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 262(b): without reasonable cause prevents or impedes any person attempting to save the life of another
#ASSERT `Under section 262, have I committed the offence of impeding an attempt to save a life` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 262, have I committed the offence of impeding an attempt to save a life` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 262: guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years, or an offence punishable on summary conviction
#ASSERT `Under section 262, how serious is impeding an attempt to save a life, and what can it cost me` EQUALS `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty` OF `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`, (LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)), TRUE

-- 263(1): every one who makes or causes to be made an opening in ice that is open to or frequented by the public is under a legal duty to guard it
#ASSERT `Under section 263(1), am I under a legal duty to guard an opening I made in ice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ice not open to the public: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 263(1), am I under a legal duty to guard an opening I made in ice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 263(2): every one who leaves an excavation on land that he owns or of which he has charge or supervision is under a legal duty to guard it
#ASSERT `Under section 263(2), am I under a legal duty to guard an excavation I left on land` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 263(2), am I under a legal duty to guard an excavation I left on land` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 263(3)(a): failing to perform a duty imposed by subsection (1) is guilty of manslaughter if the death of any person results
#ASSERT `Under section 263(3), what offence have I committed by failing to guard an opening in ice or an excavation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 263(3)(a) manslaughter`
-- 263(3)(b): an offence under section 269 if bodily harm results (here the duty is that of subsection (2), the excavation)
#ASSERT `Under section 263(3), what offence have I committed by failing to guard an opening in ice or an excavation` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 263(3)(b) an offence under section 269`
-- 263(3)(c): otherwise an offence punishable on summary conviction
#ASSERT `Under section 263(3), what offence have I committed by failing to guard an opening in ice or an excavation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 263(3)(c) an offence punishable on summary conviction`
-- no duty (the ice is not open to the public): not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 263(3), what offence have I committed by failing to guard an opening in ice or an excavation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 263(3)(a) is manslaughter: section 236(1)(b), imprisonment for life
#ASSERT `Under section 263(3), how serious is the offence of failing to guard an opening or excavation, and what can it cost me` `s 263(3)(a) manslaughter` FALSE EQUALS `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty` OF `an indictable offence`, (LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)), FALSE
-- 263(3)(b) is an offence under section 269: indictable not exceeding ten years, or summary conviction
#ASSERT `Under section 263(3), how serious is the offence of failing to guard an opening or excavation, and what can it cost me` `s 263(3)(b) an offence under section 269` FALSE EQUALS `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty` OF `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`, (LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)), TRUE
-- 263(3)(c): an offence punishable on summary conviction; no penalty of its own
#ASSERT `Under section 263(3), how serious is the offence of failing to guard an opening or excavation, and what can it cost me` `s 263(3)(c) an offence punishable on summary conviction` FALSE EQUALS `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty` OF `an offence punishable on summary conviction`, EMPTY, TRUE

§ `Violence against an intimate partner (section 263.1)`

-- 263.1(1): everyone who commits an offence in which violence is used, threatened or attempted against their intimate partner is guilty
#ASSERT `Under section 263.1(1), have I committed the offence of violence against an intimate partner` TRUE `a current spouse` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
