§ `Assaulting and disarming a peace officer (ss 270 to 270.1)`

-- A constable on duty is assaulted: a peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty.
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer` TRUE `a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace or for the service or execution of civil process` `a person in a capacity that is none of those` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The constable was not engaged in the execution of duty and the person was not aiding one: no limb holds.
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer` TRUE `a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace or for the service or execution of civil process` `a person in a capacity that is none of those` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): assault with intent to resist a lawful arrest.
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer` TRUE `a person in a capacity that is none of those` `a person in a capacity that is none of those` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c)(i): a bailiff-like person executing a process.
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer` TRUE `a person in a capacity that is none of those` `a person in a capacity that is none of those` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An officer in a capacity the definitions do not list (their lists are not closed), on duty: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer` TRUE `a person in a capacity that is none of those` `a person in a capacity that is none of those` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No assault at all: the offence needs one.
#ASSERT `Under section 270(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer` FALSE `a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace or for the service or execution of civil process` `a person in a capacity that is none of those` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 270(2), what is the most serious punishment I can face on indictment for assaulting a peace officer` EQUALS (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
#ASSERT `Under section 270(2), is assaulting a peace officer an indictable offence, a summary conviction offence or both` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
-- A weapon is used in an assault on an officer.
#ASSERT `Under section 270.01(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Bodily harm is caused.
#ASSERT `Under section 270.01(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither a weapon nor bodily harm.
#ASSERT `Under section 270.01(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A thing that is not designed for injury, not for threatening and not a firearm: the definition of weapon is an open list, so not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 270.01(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 270.01(2), what is the most serious punishment I can face on indictment for assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm` EQUALS (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
-- Wounding the complainant.
#ASSERT `Under section 270.02, do I commit aggravated assault of a peace officer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- None of wounding, maiming, disfiguring or endangering life.
#ASSERT `Under section 270.02, do I commit aggravated assault of a peace officer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 270.02, what punishment can I face for aggravated assault of a peace officer` EQUALS (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
-- The plain case.
#ASSERT `Under section 270.03, must my sentence be served consecutively to any other punishment` 270 "(1)" TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Disarming a peace officer is not one of the offences the section names.
#ASSERT `Under section 270.03, must my sentence be served consecutively to any other punishment` 270.1 "(1)" TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The plain case.
#ASSERT `Under section 270.1(1), do I commit the offence of disarming a peace officer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace or for the service or execution of civil process` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- With the peace officer's consent there is no offence.
