-- ccc10-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for the seat layer (ccc10-seat.l4): the facts a real accused would state, with the answer written by hand from the text.
-- A question that returns a Punishment is checked against a fixed s 787(1) answer (a fixture, asserted as an input, not a statement of the penalty).
-- Cases for a plain pass-through question are the layer-1 rows of the same rule seen from the seat (same facts, JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE inputs given as yes or no).

`seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`


