#ASSERT `Under section 293.1, what punishment am I liable to for forced marriage` `by indictment` `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
#ASSERT `Under section 293.1, what punishment am I liable to for forced marriage` `on summary conviction` `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty`
#ASSERT `Under section 293.2, am I guilty of the offence of marriage under the age of 16 years` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 293.2, am I guilty of the offence of marriage under the age of 16 years` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 293.2, what punishment am I liable to for marriage under the age of 16 years` `by indictment` `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
#ASSERT `Under section 293.2, what punishment am I liable to for marriage under the age of 16 years` `on summary conviction` `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty`
#ASSERT `Under section 294, am I guilty of the offence of pretending to solemnize marriage` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 294, am I guilty of the offence of pretending to solemnize marriage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 294, what punishment am I liable to for pretending to solemnize marriage` `by indictment` `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
#ASSERT `Under section 294, what punishment am I liable to for pretending to solemnize marriage` `on summary conviction` `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty`
#ASSERT `Under section 295, am I guilty of the offence of solemnizing a marriage contrary to law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 295, am I guilty of the offence of solemnizing a marriage contrary to law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 295, what punishment am I liable to for solemnizing a marriage contrary to law` `by indictment` `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
#ASSERT `Under section 295, what punishment am I liable to for solemnizing a marriage contrary to law` `on summary conviction` `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `seat fixture: the general summary conviction penalty`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ccc11 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat: cases of the seat layer ccc11-seat.l4: Part VIII.1, a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code, asking each question on facts they can state
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the provision, beside each assertion, before the run; none is copied from the code's output.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING: the text says yes / the text says no in its own words / not covered.

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE Fine
`Under section 320.19, test: the minimum fine of the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN JUST q THEN JUST (q's `minimum fine`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE Fine
`Under section 320.19, test: the maximum fine of the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN JUST q THEN JUST (q's `maximum fine`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
`Under section 320.19, test: the minimum imprisonment of the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN JUST q THEN JUST (q's `minimum imprisonment`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
`Under section 320.19, test: the maximum imprisonment of the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN JUST q THEN JUST (q's `maximum imprisonment`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN p IS A `s 320.24(2) prohibition period`
GIVETH A `Length of time`
`Under section 320.24, test: not less than` MEANS p's `s 320.24 not less than`

GIVEN p IS A `s 320.24(2) prohibition period`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Length of time`)
`Under section 320.24, test: not more than` MEANS p's `s 320.24 not more than`

GIVEN l IS A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 320.34, test: the number of items` MEANS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN JUST items THEN JUST (sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD 1) items))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.11 (the conveyance, operating it, the approved devices)`
-- arguments: my conveyance ; how I used it
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a driver of a motor vehicle operated it
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("navigated it") EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- navigating is not an act of limb (a): a car is driven
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance` "vessel" ("assisted in navigating it") EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- assisting in the navigation of a vessel (limb (b))
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance` ("railway equipment") ("participated in the direct control of its motion") EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- limb (c)
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance` "aircraft" ("had care or control of it") EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- care or control of an aircraft (limb (b))
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance` ("something else") ("drove it") EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not a conveyance: "operate means" gives no limb
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance` "bicycle" ("drove it") EQUALS NOTHING   -- not one of the listed choices: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("flew it") EQUALS NOTHING   -- not one of the listed choices: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, is what I was using a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a motor vehicle is a conveyance
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, is what I was using a conveyance` "vessel" EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a vessel
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, is what I was using a conveyance` "aircraft" EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an aircraft
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, is what I was using a conveyance` ("railway equipment") EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- railway equipment
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, is what I was using a conveyance` ("something else") EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- "conveyance means" a motor vehicle, a vessel, an aircraft or railway equipment
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, is what I was using a conveyance` "spaceship" EQUALS NOTHING   -- not one of the listed choices: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, was the device an approved screening device` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- designed for the purpose and approved
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, was the device an approved screening device` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- "approved screening device means" a device that is approved
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, was the instrument an approved instrument` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an approved instrument
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, was the instrument an approved instrument` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not an approved instrument
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, was the container an approved container` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an approved container
#ASSERT `Under section 320.11, was the container an approved container` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not an approved container

§ `Part VIII.1 -- sections 320.13 to 320.18 (the offences)`
-- arguments for 320.13(1): conveyance ; use ; the manner was dangerous
#ASSERT `Under section 320.13(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance in a manner dangerous to the public` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- drove a motor vehicle dangerously
#ASSERT `Under section 320.13(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance in a manner dangerous to the public` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the manner was not dangerous
#ASSERT `Under section 320.13(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance in a manner dangerous to the public` ("motor vehicle") ("navigated it") TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not operate a motor vehicle
#ASSERT `Under section 320.13(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance in a manner dangerous to the public` "bicycle" ("drove it") TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not one of the listed kinds: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 320.13(2), have I committed the offence of dangerous operation causing bodily harm to another person` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- dangerous driving and, as a result, bodily harm
#ASSERT `Under section 320.13(2), have I committed the offence of dangerous operation causing bodily harm to another person` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the harm was not bodily harm
#ASSERT `Under section 320.13(2), have I committed the offence of dangerous operation causing bodily harm to another person` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no harm resulted
#ASSERT `Under section 320.13(3), have I committed the offence of dangerous operation causing the death of another person` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- dangerous driving and, as a result, a death
#ASSERT `Under section 320.13(3), have I committed the offence of dangerous operation causing the death of another person` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no death resulted
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(a), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired by alcohol or a drug` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- drove while impaired
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(a), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired by alcohol or a drug` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not impaired to any degree
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(a), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired by alcohol or a drug` "vessel" ("navigated it") TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- navigated a vessel while impaired
-- arguments for 320.14(1)(b): conveyance ; use ; blood alcohol concentration ; minutes after I stopped at which the first sample was taken ; the four exception facts
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(b), have I committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 80 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- exactly 80 mg within two hours
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(b), have I committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 79 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- 79 mg is below 80
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(b), have I committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 80 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the exception of 320.14(5) applies
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(b), have I committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 76 150 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- 76 mg taken 150 minutes later: 320.31(4) adds 5 mg for one complete 30 minutes, so 81
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(b), have I committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 76 149 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- 149 minutes: no complete extra interval, so 76 stays under 80
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(b), have I committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 75 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- sample within two hours: the measured 75 stays
-- arguments for 320.14(1)(c): conveyance ; use ; my concentration ; the prescribed concentration ; the two exception facts
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(c), have I committed the offence of having a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 2 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- at the prescribed concentration
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(c), have I committed the offence of having a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 1.9 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- below it
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(c), have I committed the offence of having a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 2 2 TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the exception of 320.14(6) applies
-- arguments for 320.14(1)(d): conveyance ; use ; my alcohol ; my drug ; prescribed alcohol ; prescribed drug ; four exception facts (the drug or alcohol after; no expectation; consistent; consistent with under the prescribed)
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(d), have I committed the offence of having alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 50 1 50 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- both at the prescribed concentrations
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(d), have I committed the offence of having alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 49 1 50 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- alcohol below
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(1)(d), have I committed the offence of having alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 90 5 50 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the exception of 320.14(7) applies
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(2), have I committed the offence of impaired or over-the-limit operation causing bodily harm to another person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1) and bodily harm to another person
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(2), have I committed the offence of impaired or over-the-limit operation causing bodily harm to another person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no offence under (1)
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(2), have I committed the offence of impaired or over-the-limit operation causing bodily harm to another person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the harm was not bodily harm
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(3), have I committed the offence of impaired or over-the-limit operation causing the death of another person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1) and a death
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(3), have I committed the offence of impaired or over-the-limit operation causing the death of another person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no death
-- arguments for 320.14(4): conveyance ; use ; my concentration ; prescribed for (4) ; prescribed for (1)(c) ; two exception facts
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(4), have I committed the offence of having a low blood drug concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 3 2 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- between the two prescribed concentrations
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(4), have I committed the offence of having a low blood drug concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 5 2 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- at the (1)(c) concentration: that is paragraph (1)(c), not "less than" it
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(4), have I committed the offence of having a low blood drug concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") 1.9 2 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- below the lower concentration
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(5), does the exception for alcohol I drank after I stopped operating the conveyance apply to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all four facts of the alcohol exception
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(5), does the exception for alcohol I drank after I stopped operating the conveyance apply to me` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- I did not drink after I stopped
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(6), does the exception for a drug I took after I stopped operating the conveyance apply to me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- both facts of the drug exception
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(6), does the exception for a drug I took after I stopped operating the conveyance apply to me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- I expected to be asked for a sample
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(7), does the exception for a drug or alcohol I took after I stopped operating the conveyance apply to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all four facts of the combination exception
#ASSERT `Under section 320.14(7), does the exception for a drug or alcohol I took after I stopped operating the conveyance apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- my consumption is not consistent with the concentration
-- arguments for 320.15(1): I knew a demand was made ; I failed or refused ; I had a reasonable excuse ; the demand was one 320.27 or 320.28 allowed
#ASSERT `Under section 320.15(1), have I committed the offence of failing or refusing to comply with a demand` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- refused a lawful demand without excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 320.15(1), have I committed the offence of failing or refusing to comply with a demand` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the demand was not one the sections allowed
#ASSERT `Under section 320.15(1), have I committed the offence of failing or refusing to comply with a demand` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- with a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 320.15(2), have I committed the offence of failing or refusing to comply with a demand while knowing, or being reckless as to whether, I was involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1), knowing of an accident that resulted in bodily harm
#ASSERT `Under section 320.15(2), have I committed the offence of failing or refusing to comply with a demand while knowing, or being reckless as to whether, I was involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no such knowledge or recklessness
#ASSERT `Under section 320.15(3), have I committed the offence of failing or refusing to comply with a demand while knowing, or being reckless as to whether, I was involved in an accident that resulted in death` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1), knowing of an accident that resulted in death
#ASSERT `Under section 320.15(3), have I committed the offence of failing or refusing to comply with a demand while knowing, or being reckless as to whether, I was involved in an accident that resulted in death` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no offence under (1)
#ASSERT `Under section 320.15(4), am I barred from being convicted of another offence under section 320.15 for the same transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- barred: convicted, another offence under the section, same transaction
#ASSERT `Under section 320.15(4), am I barred from being convicted of another offence under section 320.15 for the same transaction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- a different transaction
-- arguments for 320.16(1): conveyance ; use ; I knew of the accident ; failed to stop ; failed to give name and address ; a person was injured ; failed to offer assistance ; reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 320.16(1), have I committed the offence of failing, without reasonable excuse, to stop, to give my name and address or to offer assistance after an accident involving a conveyance I was operating` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- knew of the accident and did not stop
#ASSERT `Under section 320.16(1), have I committed the offence of failing, without reasonable excuse, to stop, to give my name and address or to offer assistance after an accident involving a conveyance I was operating` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- stopped and gave my name, but did not offer assistance to an injured person
#ASSERT `Under section 320.16(1), have I committed the offence of failing, without reasonable excuse, to stop, to give my name and address or to offer assistance after an accident involving a conveyance I was operating` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- I did everything the section lists
#ASSERT `Under section 320.16(1), have I committed the offence of failing, without reasonable excuse, to stop, to give my name and address or to offer assistance after an accident involving a conveyance I was operating` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- with a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 320.16(2), have I committed the offence of failing to stop, to give my name and address or to offer assistance after an accident that I knew, or was reckless as to whether, resulted in bodily harm` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1), knowing the accident resulted in bodily harm
#ASSERT `Under section 320.16(2), have I committed the offence of failing to stop, to give my name and address or to offer assistance after an accident that I knew, or was reckless as to whether, resulted in bodily harm` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no such knowledge
#ASSERT `Under section 320.16(3), have I committed the offence of failing to stop, to give my name and address or to offer assistance after an accident that I knew, or was reckless as to whether, resulted in death` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1), knowing the accident resulted in death
#ASSERT `Under section 320.16(3), have I committed the offence of failing to stop, to give my name and address or to offer assistance after an accident that I knew, or was reckless as to whether, resulted in death` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no offence under (1)
-- arguments for 320.17: conveyance ; use ; I was being pursued ; the pursuer was a police officer or other peace officer ; I failed to stop as soon as reasonable ; reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 320.17, have I committed the offence of failing to stop a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- fled from a police officer in a motor vehicle
#ASSERT `Under section 320.17, have I committed the offence of failing to stop a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer` "vessel" ("navigated it") TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- fled in a vessel
#ASSERT `Under section 320.17, have I committed the offence of failing to stop a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer` "aircraft" ("navigated it") TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- an aircraft is neither a motor vehicle nor a vessel
#ASSERT `Under section 320.17, have I committed the offence of failing to stop a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person who pursued me was not a police officer: "peace officer includes", so not covered, not "not a peace officer"
#ASSERT `Under section 320.17, have I committed the offence of failing to stop a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- I was not being pursued
-- arguments for 320.18(1): conveyance ; use ; prohibited by an order made under the Code ; prohibited by another legal restriction ; registered in an interlock program ; I comply
#ASSERT `Under section 320.18(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- drove while prohibited by an order
#ASSERT `Under section 320.18(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the interlock exception applies to a motor vehicle
#ASSERT `Under section 320.18(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` "vessel" ("navigated it") TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the interlock exception is for a motor vehicle only
#ASSERT `Under section 320.18(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` ("motor vehicle") ("drove it") FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not prohibited
#ASSERT `Under section 320.18(2), does the interlock program exception apply to me` ("motor vehicle") TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- registered and complying
#ASSERT `Under section 320.18(2), does the interlock program exception apply to me` ("motor vehicle") FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not registered
#ASSERT `Under section 320.18(2), does the interlock program exception apply to me` "vessel" TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not a motor vehicle: the exception gives no protection

§ `Part VIII.1 -- sections 320.19 to 320.22 and 320.26 (punishment)`
-- arguments for 320.19: section ; subsection ; mode ; earlier convictions under 320.14(1)-(3) ; under 320.15 ; under former 253-255 ; my blood alcohol concentration ; the s 787(1) maximum fine ; the s 787(1) maximum months
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the minimum fine of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.14 "(1)(b)" ("by indictment") 0 0 0 130 0 0) EQUALS JUST (`a fine of` 1500)   -- first offence, 130 mg: raised by 320.19(3)
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the maximum imprisonment of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.14 "(1)(b)" ("by indictment") 0 0 0 130 0 0) EQUALS JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- indictable: not more than 10 years
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the minimum imprisonment of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.14 "(1)(b)" ("by indictment") 1 0 0 130 0 0) EQUALS JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE))   -- one earlier conviction: a second offence, 30 days
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the minimum imprisonment of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.14 "(1)" ("by indictment") 1 1 0 0 0 0) EQUALS JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 120, FALSE))   -- two earlier convictions: a subsequent offence, 120 days
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the maximum fine of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.14 "(1)" ("on summary conviction") 0 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS JUST (`a fine of` 5000)   -- summary conviction: not more than $5,000
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the minimum fine of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.15 "(1)" ("by indictment") 0 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS JUST (`a fine of` 2000)   -- 320.15(1) first offence: not less than $2,000
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the maximum fine of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.13 "(1)" ("on summary conviction") 0 0 0 0 777 3) EQUALS JUST (`a fine of` 777)   -- the summary limb is the s 787(1) penalty that the person types in
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the maximum imprisonment of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.13 "(1)" ("on summary conviction") 0 0 0 0 777 3) EQUALS JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 3, 0, FALSE))   -- the s 787(1) months typed in
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the maximum imprisonment of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.13 "(3)" ("by indictment") 0 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS JUST (`imprisonment for life`)   -- death: imprisonment for life
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the maximum fine of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.13 "(1)" ("on summary conviction") 0 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS JUST (`no fine is stated`)   -- the person types 0 for the s 787(1) figures: no fine is stated, not a fine of 0
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the maximum imprisonment of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.13 "(1)" ("on summary conviction") 0 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS JUST (`no imprisonment is stated`)   -- and no imprisonment is stated, not a term of 0 months
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the maximum imprisonment of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 320.14 "(1)" ("by agreement") 0 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the mode is not one of the two listed choices: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, test: the maximum imprisonment of the answer` (`Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` 322 "" ("by indictment") 0 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS NOTHING   -- an offence these sections do not punish: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, is my offence an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or both` 320.14 "(1)" EQUALS JUST (`an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`)   -- both
#ASSERT `Under section 320.19, is my offence an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or both` 320.14 "(4)" EQUALS JUST (`an offence punishable on summary conviction`)   -- summary only
