§ `Part VIII.1 -- sections 320.31 to 320.35 (evidence)`
-- arguments for 320.31(1): approved instrument ; qualified technician ; blank test ; calibration check ; target ; standard certified by an analyst ; minutes between samples ; first result ; second result
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(1), are the results of my breath tests conclusive proof of my blood alcohol concentration` TRUE TRUE 10 100 100 TRUE 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- every condition met at its limit
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(1), are the results of my breath tests conclusive proof of my blood alcohol concentration` TRUE TRUE 11 100 100 TRUE 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- blank test over 10 mg
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(1), are the results of my breath tests conclusive proof of my blood alcohol concentration` TRUE TRUE 10 100 100 TRUE 14 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- 14 minutes between samples
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(1), are the results of my breath tests conclusive proof of my blood alcohol concentration` TRUE TRUE 10 100 100 TRUE 15 89 110 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- rounded down 80 and 110 differ by 30
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(1), are the results of my breath tests conclusive proof of my blood alcohol concentration` TRUE TRUE 10 100 100 TRUE 15 89 109 EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- rounded down 80 and 100 differ by exactly 20
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(1), are the results of my breath tests conclusive proof of my blood alcohol concentration` TRUE TRUE 10 100 100 FALSE 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the standard was not certified by an analyst
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(1), what blood alcohol concentration do the results of my breath tests conclusively prove` TRUE TRUE 10 100 100 TRUE 15 90 100 EQUALS JUST 90   -- the lowest of the two results
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(1), what blood alcohol concentration do the results of my breath tests conclusively prove` TRUE TRUE 11 100 100 TRUE 15 90 100 EQUALS NOTHING   -- conditions not met: the results prove nothing under this subsection
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(2), is the result of the analysis of my blood sample proof of my concentration at the time the sample was taken` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an analyst, no evidence of improper analysis
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(2), is the result of the analysis of my blood sample proof of my concentration at the time the sample was taken` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- evidence of improper analysis
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(3), does this evidence tend to show that the analysis of my blood sample was performed improperly` ("the amount of alcohol or a drug I consumed") EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not evidence of improper analysis
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(3), does this evidence tend to show that the analysis of my blood sample was performed improperly` ("the rate at which it would have been absorbed or eliminated") EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not evidence of improper analysis
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(3), does this evidence tend to show that the analysis of my blood sample was performed improperly` ("a calculation based on those") EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not evidence of improper analysis
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(3), does this evidence tend to show that the analysis of my blood sample was performed improperly` ("an expert report on the machine") EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other evidence: the subsection does not address it
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(4), what blood alcohol concentration am I conclusively presumed to have had within two hours after I stopped operating the conveyance` 121 100 EQUALS JUST 100   -- one minute over two hours: no complete extra interval
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(4), what blood alcohol concentration am I conclusively presumed to have had within two hours after I stopped operating the conveyance` 150 100 EQUALS JUST 105   -- one complete interval
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(4), what blood alcohol concentration am I conclusively presumed to have had within two hours after I stopped operating the conveyance` 120 100 EQUALS NOTHING   -- exactly two hours: not "more than two hours"
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(4), what blood alcohol concentration am I conclusively presumed to have had within two hours after I stopped operating the conveyance` 150 19 EQUALS NOTHING   -- under 20 mg
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(5), is the evaluating officer's opinion admissible without qualifying the officer as an expert` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- admissible without qualifying the officer as an expert
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(5), is the evaluating officer's opinion admissible without qualifying the officer as an expert` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another opinion: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 320.31(6), is the drug presumed to have been in my body at the time I operated the conveyance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- presumed present at the time
