-- ccc13-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for every question of ccc13-seat.l4, with the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- Generated by work/gen_cases.py from the signatures and the case table work/seat_cases.py. Every expected value is decided from the text and written beside its case.
-- For an offence question the cases are: the facts that meet every element (JUST TRUE); the first element missing (JUST FALSE); the class of the offence and the greatest term
-- by indictment (from the penalty lines of the text, as the layer-1 tests state them); and, where the summary limb is left to section 787(1), the three figures the person gives.
-- The facts below use made-up figures where the text gives none (section 787(1): $5,000 and 24 months, less a day); they claim nothing about section 787(1).

§ `Fraud, ss 379 to 381`

-- Under section 379, is the thing goods
