#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE FALSE 10000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- every element met
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` FALSE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE FALSE 10000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the first element is missing: the person acts by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE FALSE 3000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` EQUALS JUST `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`      -- paragraph (b): a fraud of $3,000 on something that is not a testamentary instrument is indictable or punishable on summary conviction
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE FALSE 3000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one` EQUALS JUST (LIST `s 380(1)(b)(i) the limb`, `ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` 5000 24 TRUE)      -- paragraph (b)(i) (two years by indictment) and (b)(ii) (summary conviction, left to section 787(1))
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE FALSE 5000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` EQUALS JUST `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`      -- exactly $5,000 does not exceed $5,000: paragraph (b)
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE FALSE 5001 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` EQUALS JUST `an indictable offence`      -- $5,001 exceeds $5,000: paragraph (a)
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE TRUE 10000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` EQUALS JUST `an indictable offence`      -- a testamentary instrument worth over $5,000 is within paragraph (a) only
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE TRUE 3000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` EQUALS NOTHING      -- a testamentary instrument worth $3,000 is within paragraph (a) (a testamentary instrument) and paragraph (b) (value not over $5,000): the text gives two classes, so NOTHING (fork F3)
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE TRUE 3000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one` EQUALS NOTHING      -- the same facts: two limbs and two maxima, so no answer (fork F3)
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE TRUE 3000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- the elements of the fraud are met whatever the value
#ASSERT (`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE `real property of every description` TRUE `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` TRUE FALSE 10000 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` EQUALS JUST `an indictable offence`      -- the class the penalty provision gives (s 380(1))
