#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(1), is the activity one the order may prohibit` `s 380.2(1) seeking, obtaining or continuing employment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- employment that involves having authority over the real property, money or valuable security of another person
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(1), is the activity one the order may prohibit` `s 380.2(1) becoming or being a volunteer in any capacity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- volunteering in any capacity that involves that authority
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(1), is the activity one the order may prohibit` `s 380.2(1) seeking, obtaining or continuing employment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- a scope limit with no "only" (Periods ruling (c) of 2026-11-05): outside it the text is silent
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(1), is the activity one the order may prohibit` `s 380.2(1) an activity that is neither` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- an activity that is neither employment nor volunteering is outside what the subsection names
-- Under section 380.2(1), may the court make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(1), may the court make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "When an offender is convicted ... of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)"
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(1), may the court make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730"
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(1), may the court make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- a "when" gate: "may" function listed for a lawyer (2026-11-12 three limits, (3)); ruling (b) gives JUST FALSE
-- Under section 380.2(2), may the prohibition be for the period
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(2), may the prohibition be for the period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "any period that the court considers appropriate"
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(2), may the prohibition be for the period` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "including any period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment"
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(2), may the prohibition be for the period` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- a grant with a scope limit and no "only": a period the court does not consider appropriate is outside it (2026-11-12 three limits, (1))
-- Under section 380.2(3), may the court vary the conditions prescribed in the order
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(3), may the court vary the conditions prescribed in the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- the court that made the order, on application, after hearing the parties, in its opinion the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(3), may the court vary the conditions prescribed in the order` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- the power is given to that court (or an equivalent court if it is unable to act); a grant whose gate fails answers NOTHING (2026-11-12 three limits, (1))
