#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 393(3), is what I did the offence of fraudulently obtaining transportation, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated`      -- the greatest term by indictment the penalty provision gives (s 393(3))
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the number of limbs` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 393(3), is what I did the offence of fraudulently obtaining transportation, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS 1      -- the penalty provision states one limb (s 393(3))
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum fine on summary conviction` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 393(3), is what I did the offence of fraudulently obtaining transportation, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `a fine of` 5000      -- the summary limb is what the person gave for section 787(1)
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 393(3), is what I did the offence of fraudulently obtaining transportation, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 24, 0, TRUE)      -- the summary limb is what the person gave for section 787(1): 24 months, less a day
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 393(3), is what I did the offence of fraudulently obtaining transportation, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 5000 24 FALSE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 24, 0, FALSE)      -- the same, when the person says the term is not "less a day"
-- Under section 394(1), do I contravene subsection (1)
#ASSERT `Under section 394(1), do I contravene subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- the holder of a lease or licence who by a fraudulent device defrauds another of valuable minerals
#ASSERT `Under section 394(1), do I contravene subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING      -- "No person who is the holder of a lease or licence ... shall": a scope limit with no "only"; the text is silent about anyone else (Periods ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT `Under section 394(1), do I contravene subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING      -- neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b): the prohibition names only those acts
#ASSERT `Under section 394(1), do I contravene subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- paragraph (b) alone suffices: fraudulently conceals the amount of valuable minerals obtained
-- Under section 394(2), do I contravene subsection (2)
#ASSERT `Under section 394(2), do I contravene subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "No person, other than the owner or the owner’s agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority, shall sell any valuable mineral that is unrefined"
#ASSERT `Under section 394(2), do I contravene subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING      -- the owner is outside the prohibition; the text says nothing more about the owner (Periods ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT `Under section 394(2), do I contravene subsection (2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING      -- a person who does not sell is outside the prohibition
#ASSERT `Under section 394(2), do I contravene subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING      -- a refined mineral is outside the prohibition
-- Under section 394(3), do I contravene subsection (3)
#ASSERT `Under section 394(3), do I contravene subsection (3)` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "No person shall buy any valuable mineral that is unrefined ... from anyone who the person has reason to believe is not the owner"
#ASSERT `Under section 394(3), do I contravene subsection (3)` FALSE TRUE TRUE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING      -- a person who does not buy is outside the prohibition
#ASSERT `Under section 394(3), do I contravene subsection (3)` TRUE FALSE TRUE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING      -- a refined mineral is outside the prohibition
#ASSERT `Under section 394(3), do I contravene subsection (3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a mineral` 10000 EQUALS NOTHING      -- the prohibition is limited to a purchase from one the person has reason to believe is not the owner
-- Under section 394(4)(a), is it presumed, in the case of a sale, that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority
#ASSERT `Under section 394(4)(a), is it presumed, in the case of a sale, that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary, it is presumed that (a) in the case of a sale, the seller is not the owner"
#ASSERT `Under section 394(4)(a), is it presumed, in the case of a sale, that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the presumption holds only "in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary"
#ASSERT `Under section 394(4)(a), is it presumed, in the case of a sale, that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "In any proceeding in relation to subsection (2) or (3)": a proceeding scope read as a "where" gate (Periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05); a sale presumption needs a proceeding under (2)
-- Under section 394(4)(b), is it presumed, in the case of a purchase, that the purchaser had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority
#ASSERT `Under section 394(4)(b), is it presumed, in the case of a purchase, that the purchaser had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary, it is presumed that (b) in the case of a purchase, the purchaser ... had reason to believe"
#ASSERT `Under section 394(4)(b), is it presumed, in the case of a purchase, that the purchaser had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the presumption holds only "in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary"
#ASSERT `Under section 394(4)(b), is it presumed, in the case of a purchase, that the purchaser had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "In any proceeding in relation to subsection (2) or (3)": a proceeding scope read as a "where" gate (Periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05)
-- Under section 394(5), am I guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3), and what are its class and punishments
#ASSERT (`Under section 394(5), am I guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3), and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a mineral` 10000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- every element met
