-- Under section 395(1), may the justice issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1), may the justice issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` TRUE `a mayor` `an officer of customs or excise` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- an information in writing laid under oath before a justice by a peace officer, and the justice is satisfied there are reasonable grounds
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1), may the justice issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` FALSE `a mayor` `an officer of customs or excise` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- a "may" grant whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (2026-11-12 three limits, (1))
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1), may the justice issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` TRUE `a mayor` `an officer of customs or excise` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- the same: the justice must be "satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe"
-- Under section 395(1), does the warrant authorize the officer to search
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1), does the warrant authorize the officer to search` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "authorizing a peace officer or a public officer, if the public officer is named in it"
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1), does the warrant authorize the officer to search` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- a public officer named in the warrant
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1), does the warrant authorize the officer to search` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- a public officer is authorized "if the public officer is named in it"; an unnamed one is outside the grant, which has no "only"
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1), does the warrant authorize the officer to search` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- an officer who is neither is outside the grant
-- Under section 395(1.1), does the officer who executes the warrant have the authority the subsection requires
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1.1), does the officer who executes the warrant have the authority the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "A public officer named in the warrant, or any peace officer, who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed"
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1.1), does the officer who executes the warrant have the authority the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "must have authority": the text states the requirement and a duty not met is a no
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1.1), does the officer who executes the warrant have the authority the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- the requirement is stated for a named public officer and a peace officer; another officer is outside it
-- Under section 395(1.1), may the warrant be executed at the place
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1.1), may the warrant be executed at the place` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada"
#ASSERT `Under section 395(1.1), may the warrant be executed at the place` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- a grant limited to places in Canada, with no "only": outside Canada the text is silent
