-- Under section 402.2(4), may the accused be tried and punished by the court
#ASSERT `Under section 402.2(4), may the accused be tried and punished by the court` TRUE `s 402.2(4) the place where the accused is found` EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "may be tried and punished by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where ... the accused is found"
#ASSERT `Under section 402.2(4), may the accused be tried and punished by the court` TRUE `s 402.2(4) the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed` EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed"
#ASSERT `Under section 402.2(4), may the accused be tried and punished by the court` FALSE `s 402.2(4) the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed` EQUALS NOTHING      -- a grant limited to a court having jurisdiction; outside it the text is silent (2026-11-12 three limits, (1))
#ASSERT `Under section 402.2(4), may the accused be tried and punished by the court` TRUE `s 402.2(4) a place that is none of those` EQUALS NOTHING      -- a place other than the four the subsection names is outside the grant, which has no "only"
-- Under section 402.2(4), does the subsection bar the proceeding for want of the consent of the Attorney General of the province
#ASSERT `Under section 402.2(4), does the subsection bar the proceeding for want of the consent of the Attorney General of the province` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "no proceeding in respect of the offence shall be commenced in a province without the consent of the Attorney General of that province if the offence is alleged to have been committed outside that province"
#ASSERT `Under section 402.2(4), does the subsection bar the proceeding for want of the consent of the Attorney General of the province` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- with the consent the subsection says nothing more (Periods ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT `Under section 402.2(4), does the subsection bar the proceeding for want of the consent of the Attorney General of the province` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- a bar that applies "if the offence is alleged to have been committed outside that province": an "if" scope read as a "where" gate (Periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05)
