-- Under section 412(2), is the thing forfeited
#ASSERT `Under section 412(2), is the thing forfeited` 407 "" TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "Anything by means of or in relation to which a person commits an offence under section 407 ... is, unless the court otherwise orders, forfeited on the conviction"
#ASSERT `Under section 412(2), is the thing forfeited` 411 "" TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- section 411 is named
#ASSERT `Under section 412(2), is the thing forfeited` 407 "" TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "unless the court otherwise orders": the text closes it in its own words
#ASSERT `Under section 412(2), is the thing forfeited` 407 "" TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "forfeited on the conviction of that person for that offence"
#ASSERT `Under section 412(2), is the thing forfeited` 380 "" TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- "an offence under section 407, 408, 409, 410 or 411": any other offence is outside the subsection
-- Under section 414, is the evidence proof that the goods were made or produced in the country from which they were shipped
#ASSERT `Under section 414, is the evidence proof that the goods were made or produced in the country from which they were shipped` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "Where, in proceedings under this Part, the alleged offence relates to imported goods, evidence that the goods were shipped to Canada from a place outside Canada is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof"
#ASSERT `Under section 414, is the evidence proof that the goods were made or produced in the country from which they were shipped` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- works only "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
#ASSERT `Under section 414, is the evidence proof that the goods were made or produced in the country from which they were shipped` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- without that evidence the section is silent
#ASSERT `Under section 414, is the evidence proof that the goods were made or produced in the country from which they were shipped` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "Where, in proceedings under this Part, the alleged offence relates to imported goods": a "where" gate (Periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05)

