-- Under section 423.1(1), do I contravene subsection (1)
#ASSERT `Under section 423.1(1), do I contravene subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a group of persons or the general public, in order to impede the administration of criminal justice` `a member of the Senate, of the House of Commons, of a legislative assembly or of a municipal council` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "No person shall, without lawful authority, engage in any conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in a group of persons or the general public in order to impede the administration of criminal justice"
#ASSERT `Under section 423.1(1), do I contravene subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a group of persons or the general public, in order to impede the administration of criminal justice` `a member of the Senate, of the House of Commons, of a legislative assembly or of a municipal council` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- a prohibition worded "without lawful authority"; for conduct with lawful authority the text is silent (Periods ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT `Under section 423.1(1), do I contravene subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE `s 423.1(1) a group of persons or the general public, in order to impede the administration of criminal justice` `a member of the Senate, of the House of Commons, of a legislative assembly or of a municipal council` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- the prohibition is limited to conduct "with the intent to provoke a state of fear"
#ASSERT `Under section 423.1(1), do I contravene subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a target that is none of those` `a member of the Senate, of the House of Commons, of a legislative assembly or of a municipal council` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- a target other than the three named is outside the prohibition
