#ASSERT (`Under section 424, is what I did the offence of a threat against an internationally protected person, and what are its class and punishments` FALSE 235 "" `a head of state, including a member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, while in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the first element is missing: the person threatens to commit the offence
#ASSERT (`Under section 424, is what I did the offence of a threat against an internationally protected person, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE 380 "" `a head of state, including a member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, while in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "threatens to commit an offence under section 235, 236, 266, ... or 279.1" and no other: the section named is not in the list (fork F1)
#ASSERT (`Under section 424, is what I did the offence of a threat against an internationally protected person, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE 431 "" `a person who is none of those` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "or who threatens to commit an offence under section 431": no internationally protected person is needed for that threat
#ASSERT (`Under section 424, is what I did the offence of a threat against an internationally protected person, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE 235 "" `a person who is none of those` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- a threat of an offence under section 235 must be "against an internationally protected person"; this person is not one
#ASSERT (`Under section 424, is what I did the offence of a threat against an internationally protected person, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE 235 "" `a head of state, including a member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, while in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` EQUALS JUST `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`      -- the class the penalty provision gives (s 424)
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 424, is what I did the offence of a threat against an internationally protected person, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE 235 "" `a head of state, including a member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, while in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`      -- the greatest term by indictment the penalty provision gives (s 424)
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum fine on summary conviction` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 424, is what I did the offence of a threat against an internationally protected person, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE 235 "" `a head of state, including a member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, while in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `a fine of` 5000      -- the summary limb is what the person gave for section 787(1)
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 424, is what I did the offence of a threat against an internationally protected person, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE 235 "" `a head of state, including a member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, while in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 24, 0, TRUE)      -- the summary limb is what the person gave for section 787(1): 24 months, less a day
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 424, is what I did the offence of a threat against an internationally protected person, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE 235 "" `a head of state, including a member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, while in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` TRUE 5000 24 FALSE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 24, 0, FALSE)      -- the same, when the person says the term is not "less a day"
-- Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments
#ASSERT (`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 235 "" `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- every element met
#ASSERT (`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` FALSE TRUE 235 "" `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the first element is missing: the person threatens to commit the offence
#ASSERT (`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE FALSE 235 "" `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "with intent to compel any person, group of persons, state or any international or intergovernmental organization to do or refrain from doing any act": read as governing both threats (fork F11)
#ASSERT (`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 380 "" `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the section named is not in the list (fork F1)
#ASSERT (`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 431.1 "" `a person who is none of those` `appointed in none of the ways (a), (b) or (c) of the definition of associated personnel` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "or threatens to commit an offence under section 431.1": no member of the personnel is needed for that threat
#ASSERT (`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 235 "" `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` EQUALS JUST `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`      -- the class the penalty provision gives (s 424.1)
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 235 "" `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`      -- the greatest term by indictment the penalty provision gives (s 424.1)
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum fine on summary conviction` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 235 "" `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `a fine of` 5000      -- the summary limb is what the person gave for section 787(1)
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 235 "" `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` TRUE 5000 24 TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 24, 0, TRUE)      -- the summary limb is what the person gave for section 787(1): 24 months, less a day
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 424.1, is what I did the offence of a threat against United Nations or associated personnel, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE 235 "" `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` TRUE 5000 24 FALSE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 24, 0, FALSE)      -- the same, when the person says the term is not "less a day"
