-- Under section 426(4), is the person a principal
#ASSERT `Under section 426(4), is the person a principal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "principal includes an employer": a principal is a principal
#ASSERT `Under section 426(4), is the person a principal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "principal includes an employer"
#ASSERT `Under section 426(4), is the person a principal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- "includes": the list is not closed, so the text does not say another person is not a principal
-- Under section 426(4), is the person an agent
#ASSERT `Under section 426(4), is the person an agent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "agent includes an employee": an agent is an agent
#ASSERT `Under section 426(4), is the person an agent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "agent includes an employee"
#ASSERT `Under section 426(4), is the person an agent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- "includes": the list is not closed, so the text does not say another person is not an agent

§ `Mischief, ss 428 to 432`

-- Under section 428, is the thing property
#ASSERT `Under section 428, is the thing property` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- every fact the question asks is true
#ASSERT `Under section 428, is the thing property` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the first fact is false: the thing is real or personal corporeal property
-- Under section 429(1), am I deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event
#ASSERT `Under section 429(1), am I deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "Every one who causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is his duty to do, knowing that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event and being reckless whether the event occurs or not, shall be deemed ... wilfully to have caused"
#ASSERT `Under section 429(1), am I deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- the subsection deems one case wilful and says nothing of a person outside it
#ASSERT `Under section 429(1), am I deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- the same: the deeming needs the knowledge
#ASSERT `Under section 429(1), am I deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- the same: the deeming needs recklessness
-- Under section 429(2), is it the case that the person shall not be convicted of the offence
#ASSERT `Under section 429(2), is it the case that the person shall not be convicted of the offence` 430 "" TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "A person shall not be convicted of an offence under sections 430 to 446 if they act with legal justification or excuse or colour of right"
#ASSERT `Under section 429(2), is it the case that the person shall not be convicted of the offence` 446 "" TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- section 446 is the last section of the range
#ASSERT `Under section 429(2), is it the case that the person shall not be convicted of the offence` 435 "" FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- this subsection gives no protection on these facts (a "no conviction if" saving, read as in Delegated ruling (b) of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT `Under section 429(2), is it the case that the person shall not be convicted of the offence` 380 "" TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- "an offence under sections 430 to 446": any other offence is outside the subsection
-- Under section 429(3)(a), does the person’s partial interest not prevent guilt of the offence
#ASSERT `Under section 429(3)(a), does the person’s partial interest not prevent guilt of the offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- every fact the question asks is true
#ASSERT `Under section 429(3)(a), does the person’s partial interest not prevent guilt of the offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the first fact is false: it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing
-- Under section 429(3)(b), does the person’s total interest not prevent guilt of the offence
#ASSERT `Under section 429(3)(b), does the person’s total interest not prevent guilt of the offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- every fact the question asks is true
#ASSERT `Under section 429(3)(b), does the person’s total interest not prevent guilt of the offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the first fact is false: it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing
-- Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "Every one commits mischief who wilfully destroys or damages property"
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- not wilful and not deemed wilful by section 429(1): the deeming subsection says nothing of a person outside its case
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- wilful because deemed so by section 429(1): causes the event, knowing the act will probably cause it, and being reckless
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) an act that is none of those, in relation to property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "Every one commits mischief who wilfully" does one of the four acts: any other act is not mischief (fork F1)
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` FALSE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- section 428: "property means real or personal corporeal property"
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- section 430(6): "No person commits mischief ... by reason only that he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and himself to agree"
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- section 430(7): "No person commits mischief ... by reason only that he attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information"
-- Under section 430(1.1), is what I did mischief in relation to computer data
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1.1), is what I did mischief in relation to computer data` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1.1) destroys or alters computer data` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "Everyone commits mischief who wilfully destroys or alters computer data"
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1.1), is what I did mischief in relation to computer data` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1.1) destroys or alters computer data` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- not wilful and not deemed wilful by section 429(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1.1), is what I did mischief in relation to computer data` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1.1) an act that is none of those, in relation to computer data` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- any other act is not mischief in relation to computer data (fork F1)
#ASSERT `Under section 430(1.1), is what I did mischief in relation to computer data` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1.1) destroys or alters computer data` FALSE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- section 430(8): "computer data has the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2)"; this is not computer data
-- Under section 430(2), is what I did the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life, and what are its class and punishments
#ASSERT (`Under section 430(2), is what I did the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 430(1.1) destroys or alters computer data` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- every element met
#ASSERT (`Under section 430(2), is what I did the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 430(1.1) destroys or alters computer data` TRUE FALSE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the first element is missing: the mischief causes actual danger to life
#ASSERT (`Under section 430(2), is what I did the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 430(1.1) destroys or alters computer data` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` EQUALS JUST `an indictable offence`      -- the class the penalty provision gives (s 430(2))
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 430(2), is what I did the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 430(1.1) destroys or alters computer data` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS `imprisonment for life`      -- the greatest term by indictment the penalty provision gives (s 430(2))
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the number of limbs` (`ccc13 test the limbs of the answer` ((`Under section 430(2), is what I did the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 430(1) destroys or damages property` TRUE `s 430(6) the person stops work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree on any matter relating to their employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 430(1.1) destroys or alters computer data` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one`)) EQUALS 1      -- the penalty provision states one limb (s 430(2))
