-- Under section 445.1(3), is the evidence proof that the pain, suffering or injury was caused or permitted wilfully
#ASSERT `Under section 445.1(3), is the evidence proof that the pain, suffering or injury was caused or permitted wilfully` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "For the purposes of proceedings under paragraph (1)(a), evidence that a person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal ... is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the pain, suffering or injury was caused or was permitted to be caused wilfully"
#ASSERT `Under section 445.1(3), is the evidence proof that the pain, suffering or injury was caused or permitted wilfully` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- works only "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
#ASSERT `Under section 445.1(3), is the evidence proof that the pain, suffering or injury was caused or permitted wilfully` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- without that evidence the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `Under section 445.1(3), is the evidence proof that the pain, suffering or injury was caused or permitted wilfully` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "For the purposes of proceedings under paragraph (1)(a)": a proceeding scope read as a "where" gate (Periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05)
