#ASSERT `Under section 445.1(4), is the evidence proof that the accused encouraged, aided or assisted at the fighting or baiting` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- "For the purpose of proceedings under paragraph (1)(b), evidence that an accused was present at the fighting or baiting of animals or birds is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that he or she encouraged, aided or assisted"
#ASSERT `Under section 445.1(4), is the evidence proof that the accused encouraged, aided or assisted at the fighting or baiting` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- works only "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
#ASSERT `Under section 445.1(4), is the evidence proof that the accused encouraged, aided or assisted at the fighting or baiting` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- without that evidence the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `Under section 445.1(4), is the evidence proof that the accused encouraged, aided or assisted at the fighting or baiting` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "For the purpose of proceedings under paragraph (1)(b)": a proceeding scope read as a "where" gate (Periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05)
