-- ccc15-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for the seat layer ccc15-seat.l4: the questions Part XIV (Jurisdiction) answers for a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence.
-- Each case is stated with the facts a real person in that seat would state; every expected value is written here from the text before the run (decided by reading the section),
-- beside its assertion, and not copied from the encoding's output. JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text's own no; NOTHING is not covered (never no).


§ `Part XIV -- which court may try me (ss 468 to 471)`

-- Anna is charged with murder (section 235) in Ontario, and is to be tried in the Superior Court of Justice.
#ASSERT `Under section 468, does a superior court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Ontario Court of Justice is not a superior court of criminal jurisdiction: section 468 does not speak to it.
#ASSERT `Under section 468, does a superior court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` `the Ontario Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A summary conviction offence is not "any indictable offence".
#ASSERT `Under section 468, does a superior court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario `an offence punishable on summary conviction` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 468, does a superior court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 235 murder is listed in section 469; so is conspiring to commit murder; attempted murder (section 239) is not, and nor is an attempt charged against section 235.
#ASSERT `Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469` 235 `s 469 the charge is of conspiring to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469` 239 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469` 235 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Bribery under section 119 by a judge is listed; by anyone else it is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469` 119 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469` 119 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Being an accessory after the fact to murder is listed; a war crime under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act is listed.
#ASSERT `Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469` 235 `s 469 the charge is of being an accessory after the fact to the offence named` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469` 4 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Bernard is charged with theft (section 334, indictable) and is before the Ontario Court of Justice: a court of criminal jurisdiction may try it.
#ASSERT `Under section 469, does a court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` `the Ontario Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` 334 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Charged with murder, the same court may not try it: section 469 lists it.
#ASSERT `Under section 469, does a court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` `the Ontario Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Superior Court of Justice is not a court of criminal jurisdiction: section 469 does not speak to it.
#ASSERT `Under section 469, does a court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` 334 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A summary conviction offence before the Ontario Court of Justice: section 469 speaks of an indictable offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 469, does a court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` `the Ontario Court of Justice` Ontario `an offence punishable on summary conviction` 334 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 470: Anna was arrested in the court's area, so the Superior Court of Justice is competent.
#ASSERT `Under section 470, is the court competent to try me for the offence` `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Ordered to be tried by that court, not found, arrested or in custody there: competent.
#ASSERT `Under section 470, is the court competent to try me for the offence` `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- None of the connections: the section's "if" limbs are unmet: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 470, is the court competent to try me for the offence` `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Another provision of the Code takes the competence away: this section does not decide.
#ASSERT `Under section 470, is the court competent to try me for the offence` `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Ontario Court of Justice has no power to try murder (section 469), so section 470 does not make it competent.
#ASSERT `Under section 470, is the court competent to try me for the offence` `the Ontario Court of Justice` Ontario `an indictable offence` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 471: an indictable offence is tried by judge and jury unless the law expressly provides otherwise.
#ASSERT `Under section 471, must I be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 471, must I be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 471, must I be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an offence punishable on summary conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Part XIV -- trial without a jury (s 473)`

-- Anna (murder, section 235) and the Attorney General both consent to trial without a jury by a judge of the Superior Court of Justice.
#ASSERT `Under section 473(1), may I be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Attorney General has not consented: the section's limit "with the consent of the accused and the Attorney General" is not met.
#ASSERT `Under section 473(1), may I be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario EQUALS NOTHING
-- Theft (section 334) is not listed in section 469, so section 473(1) does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Under section 473(1), may I be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` 334 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario EQUALS NOTHING
-- The trial court is the Ontario Court of Justice, not a superior court.
#ASSERT `Under section 473(1), may I be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `the Ontario Court of Justice` Ontario EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 473(1.1), may the judge order that another offence be tried by that judge together with the offence listed in section 469` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 473(1.1), may the judge order that another offence be tried by that judge together with the offence listed in section 469` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario EQUALS NOTHING
-- Anna changes her mind and the Attorney General does not agree: the withdrawal is barred. If both agree it is not. Without a consent given under (1) the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `Under section 473(2), is the withdrawal of my consent to be tried without a jury barred` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 473(2), is the withdrawal of my consent to be tried without a jury barred` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 473(2), is the withdrawal of my consent to be tried without a jury barred` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Superior Court of Justice` Ontario FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Part XIV -- adjournment when no jury is summoned (s 474)`

-- The clerk may adjourn on the opening day when no jury panel is to be summoned and no judge is present.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day when no jury panel is to be summoned` `a clerk of the court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE; question retitled to ask what the function answers, expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day, on the opening day of a term or sittings for which no jury panel is to be summoned, if no judge is present to preside` `a clerk of the court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A judge is present: the "if a judge is not present" limit fails.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day when no jury panel is to be summoned` `a clerk of the court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; question retitled to ask what the function answers, expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day, on the opening day of a term or sittings for which no jury panel is to be summoned, if no judge is present to preside` `a clerk of the court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day when no jury panel is to be summoned` `a clerk of the court` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; question retitled to ask what the function answers, expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day, on the opening day of a term or sittings for which no jury panel is to be summoned, if no judge is present to preside` `a clerk of the court` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day when no jury panel is to be summoned` `a clerk of the court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; question retitled to ask what the function answers, expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day, on the opening day of a term or sittings for which no jury panel is to be summoned, if no judge is present to preside` `a clerk of the court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day when no jury panel is to be summoned` `a person who neither is a clerk of the court nor performs a clerk of the court's duties` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; question retitled to ask what the function answers, expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day, on the opening day of a term or sittings for which no jury panel is to be summoned, if no judge is present to preside` `a person who neither is a clerk of the court nor performs a clerk of the court's duties` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 474(2), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day on a judge's instructions` `a clerk of the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 474(2), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day on a judge's instructions` `a clerk of the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Part XIV -- if I abscond during my trial (s 475)`

-- Carl absconds in the middle of his trial. He is deemed to have waived his right to be present; the court may go on to judgment; if he is found guilty it may sentence him in his absence.
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1)(a), am I deemed to have waived my right to be present at my trial if I abscond` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1)(a), am I deemed to have waived my right to be present at my trial if I abscond` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1)(b)(i), may the court continue my trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict in my absence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1)(b)(i), may the court continue my trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict in my absence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1)(b)(i), may the court sentence me in my absence if it finds me guilty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1)(b)(i), may the court sentence me in my absence if it finds me guilty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- If a warrant in Form 7 is issued, the court may instead adjourn to await his appearance, and may later continue if satisfied that it is no longer in the interests of justice to wait.
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1)(b)(ii), may the court adjourn my trial to await my appearance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1)(b)(ii), may the court adjourn my trial to await my appearance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1), may the court continue my trial at any time after adjourning it to await my appearance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1), may the court continue my trial at any time after adjourning it to await my appearance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 475(1), may the court continue my trial at any time after adjourning it to await my appearance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The court continues the trial: it may draw an adverse inference from his absconding. Carl reappears: he is barred from having what was done in his absence re-opened unless the court is satisfied that exceptional circumstances make it in the interests of justice. His counsel keeps any authority to act.
#ASSERT `Under section 475(2), may the court draw an inference adverse to me from the fact that I absconded` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(2), may the court draw an inference adverse to me from the fact that I absconded` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(3), am I barred from having the part of my trial conducted in my absence re-opened` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(3), am I barred from having the part of my trial conducted in my absence re-opened` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(3), am I barred from having the part of my trial conducted in my absence re-opened` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(4), does the section preserve my counsel's authority to continue to act for me when I abscond and my trial continues` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 475(4), does the section preserve my counsel's authority to continue to act for me when I abscond and my trial continues` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Part XIV -- where my offence is treated as committed (s 476)`

-- Dan's offence happened on a bridge between two counties; the county asked about is one of those the bridge joins.
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat on water or on a bridge between two or more territorial divisions` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat the water or bridge lies between it and another territorial division` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another county, not one the bridge joins: section 476(a) deems it committed in the divisions the bridge lies between and says nothing of any other.
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat on water or on a bridge between two or more territorial divisions` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat it is connected to my offence in none of these ways` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Eve's offence was committed 500 metres from the boundary between two townships (within five hundred metres), and 501 metres (outside).
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat on or near the boundary of two or more territorial divisions` 500 FALSE `s 476 seat the boundary on or near which the offence was committed is a boundary of it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat on or near the boundary of two or more territorial divisions` 501 FALSE `s 476 seat the boundary on or near which the offence was committed is a boundary of it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat on or near the boundary of two or more territorial divisions` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat the boundary on or near which the offence was committed is a boundary of it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Begun in one county and finished in another: deemed committed in either.
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat commenced in one territorial division and completed in another` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat the offence was commenced in it, or completed in it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Frank's offence was in a vehicle on a journey; the county asked about is one the vehicle passed through.
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat in or on a vehicle on a journey, or on a vessel on a navigable river, canal or inland water` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat the vehicle or vessel passed through it on the journey or voyage` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The road is itself the boundary between two counties, and the county asked about is one of them.
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat in or on a vehicle on a journey, or on a vessel on a navigable river, canal or inland water` 0 TRUE `s 476 seat the road or water the vehicle or vessel passed along is a boundary of it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The road is not a boundary, so the second limb of paragraph (c) does not apply; the first limb applies (a vehicle on a journey) but names the divisions the vehicle passed through, and nothing says this one is: not covered. The second limb alone answers JUST FALSE (asserted at paragraph level in ccc15-tests-special.l4); the section answers for all its paragraphs, so the aggregate is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat in or on a vehicle on a journey, or on a vessel on a navigable river, canal or inland water` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat the road or water the vehicle or vessel passed along is a boundary of it` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Gina's offence was committed in an aircraft; the flight commenced in the county asked about, passed over it, or ended in it.
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat in an aircraft in the course of a flight` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat the flight commenced in it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat in an aircraft in the course of a flight` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat the aircraft passed over it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat in an aircraft in the course of a flight` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat the flight ended in it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An offence in respect of the mail in door-to-door delivery: deemed committed in any county the mail was carried through.
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat in respect of the mail in the course of its door-to-door delivery` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat the mail was carried through it on that delivery` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An offence somewhere else: no paragraph of section 476 applies.
#ASSERT `Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` `s 476 seat somewhere else` 0 FALSE `s 476 seat it is connected to my offence in none of these ways` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Part XIV -- offences at sea and outside Canada (ss 477 to 477.4)`

-- Section 477(1): a sailing yacht is a vessel designed for marine navigation, with or without an engine: a ship for sections 477.1 to 477.4. A houseboat moored permanently and not capable of navigation is not within the definition's description: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 477(1), is the vessel a ship for sections 477.1 to 477.4` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 477(1), is the vessel a ship for sections 477.1 to 477.4` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 477(2): sections 477.1 to 477.4 do not limit another Act or a court's other jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Under section 477(2), do sections 477.1 to 477.4 limit the operation of another Act of Parliament or a court's jurisdiction apart from them` `s 477(2) the operation of another Act of Parliament` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 477(2), do sections 477.1 to 477.4 limit the operation of another Act of Parliament or a court's jurisdiction apart from them` `s 477(2) the jurisdiction that a court may exercise apart from sections 477.1 to 477.4` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 477(2), do sections 477.1 to 477.4 limit the operation of another Act of Parliament or a court's jurisdiction apart from them` `s 477(2) something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Hana, a Canadian citizen, did the act outside Canada on a registered yacht: it would be an offence under a federal law if done in Canada; the ship is registered under an Act of Parliament.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.1, am I deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The yacht is not registered, and nothing else applies: none of (a) to (e).
#ASSERT `Under section 477.1, am I deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In the exclusive economic zone, fishing, against a Canadian citizen: paragraph (a)'s three conditions.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.1, am I deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside the territory of any state, by a Canadian citizen.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.1, am I deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Hot pursuit.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.1, am I deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- It would not be an offence under a federal law if it occurred in Canada: the section does not speak.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.1, am I deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The thing is not a vessel, boat or craft: section 477(1) "includes" does not say it is not a ship, so paragraph (c) is not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.1, am I deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Ivan, not a Canadian citizen, is prosecuted by indictment for an offence in the territorial sea of Canada alleged to have been committed on a foreign-registered ship. Proceedings commenced 1 January 2026.
-- The Attorney General of Canada consented on 9 January 2026 (the eighth day): in time, so not barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent` TRUE FALSE TRUE `by indictment` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 9 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Consent on 10 January (the ninth day): too late, barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent` TRUE FALSE TRUE `by indictment` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent yet and it is the eighth day: not yet barred; no consent on the ninth day: barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent` TRUE FALSE TRUE `by indictment` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 9 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent` TRUE FALSE TRUE `by indictment` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Summary conviction: subsection (1) does not apply. A Canadian citizen: the condition is unmet.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent` TRUE FALSE TRUE `on summary conviction` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent` TRUE TRUE TRUE `by indictment` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The offence was not in or on the territorial sea: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent` FALSE FALSE TRUE `by indictment` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The last day for the consent: eight days after 1 January 2026 is 9 January 2026; after 25 February 2024 (a leap year) it is 4 March 2024.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), what is the last day on which the Attorney General of Canada's consent may be obtained` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 9 1 2026; question retitled to ask what the function answers, expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), what is the last day by which the Attorney General of Canada's consent must be obtained for the proceedings to be continued` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 9 1 2026
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), what is the last day on which the Attorney General of Canada's consent may be obtained` (Date 25 2 2024) EQUALS Date 4 3 2024; question retitled to ask what the function answers, expected value unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(1), what is the last day by which the Attorney General of Canada's consent must be obtained for the proceedings to be continued` (Date 25 2 2024) EQUALS Date 4 3 2024
-- Section 477.2(2): jurisdiction only by virtue of 477.1(a) or (b); a foreign national on a foreign ship; consent on the ninth day: barred; on the eighth: not.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(2), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(2), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 9 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(2), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(2), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)` FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 477.2(3): jurisdiction only by virtue of 477.1(d) or (e): no condition on the accused or the ship.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(3), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(3), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 9 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(3), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The consent must be filed with the clerk of the court in which the proceedings were instituted.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(4), has the Attorney General's consent been filed with the clerk of the court as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(4), has the Attorney General's consent been filed with the clerk of the court as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 477.2(4), has the Attorney General's consent been filed with the clerk of the court as the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A power of arrest at the place where the act occurred, section 477.1 applying: yes. On the seas in hot pursuit: yes, except in another state's territorial sea.
#ASSERT `Under section 477.3(1), may a power of arrest, entry, search or seizure be exercised at this place` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 477.3(1)(a) the place where the act or omission occurred` EQUALS JUST TRUE
