-- ccc17-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for the seat layer ccc17-seat.l4: one or more cases per question, with the facts a real person in the seat would state. Expected values are written from the text
-- (JUST TRUE = yes on the text's own words; JUST FALSE = the text says no; NOTHING = not covered), and a case outside the encoding (an explicit NOTHING) for each question that has one.
-- The facts and expected values were written by hand from the text; the question names were copied from the seat layer by a script that checked each one exists exactly once.

-- Under section 487.05(1), may...
-- all limbs met
