-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ccc19 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc19-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for the questions of ccc19-seat.l4 (Criminal Code (Canada), Part XV.1 Unreasonable Delay), with the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text, before the run, and the comment beside each case says which words decide it. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- Dates: a hearing on 1 June 2026; 2 April 2026 is exactly 60 days before it, 3 April 59 days before, 1 April 61 days before (checked by hand).
-- Every question has at least one case answered JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE and, where the section can leave the case outside it, one answered NOTHING.


§ `s 492.21 -- Under section 492.21, is the delay in my case an unreasonable delay for the purposes of Part XV.1`
-- Maya has waited far longer than the reasonable time under paragraph 11(b): an unreasonable delay (the definition's "means").
#ASSERT `Under section 492.21, is the delay in my case an unreasonable delay for the purposes of Part XV.1` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Her co-accused's case has not exceeded the reasonable time: not an unreasonable delay.
#ASSERT `Under section 492.21, is the delay in my case an unreasonable delay for the purposes of Part XV.1` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 492.21 -- Under section 492.21, is the body I am before a court for the purposes of Part XV.1`
-- She is before the court that has an application for a determination of unreasonable delay in front of it: a "court" under the Part.
#ASSERT `Under section 492.21, is the body I am before a court for the purposes of Part XV.1` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- She is before a trial court with no such application filed: not a "court" as the Part defines it.
#ASSERT `Under section 492.21, is the body I am before a court for the purposes of Part XV.1` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A body that is not a court at all (a tribunal) with such an application: not a "court".
#ASSERT `Under section 492.21, is the body I am before a court for the purposes of Part XV.1` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 492.22 -- Under section 492.22, does a finding of unreasonable delay deprive the court seized with my proceedings of jurisdiction`
-- The court has found unreasonable delay in her proceedings and is seized with them: does it lose jurisdiction over her, the accused? The text says it does not.
#ASSERT `Under section 492.22, does a finding of unreasonable delay deprive the court seized with my proceedings of jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE `s 492.22 the accused` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same, asked about the offence.
