-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ccc21 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc21-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for the seat questions of ccc21-seat.l4 (Parts XVII to XIX): the facts a person who is or may be accused would state, and the answer the text gives.
-- Expected values are written from the text, beside each case. Arguments are in the order of each question's inputs. JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is no (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING is "not covered".
-- Dates: 1 March 2026 is 59 days after 1 January 2026, and 2 March is 60 days after.


-- section 530(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 530(1), must the court grant an order that I be tried before a justice or judge who speaks my official language` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- My language is French. I applied a month before the appearance at which my trial date is set.
#ASSERT `Under section 530(1), must the court grant an order that I be tried before a justice or judge who speaks my official language` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I applied on the day of that appearance: "not later than the time of the appearance".
#ASSERT `Under section 530(1), must the court grant an order that I be tried before a justice or judge who speaks my official language` TRUE TRUE (Date 2 4 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I applied the day after that appearance: too late.
#ASSERT `Under section 530(1), must the court grant an order that I be tried before a justice or judge who speaks my official language` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I have not applied: the subsection speaks of "On application by an accused".
#ASSERT `Under section 530(1), must the court grant an order that I be tried before a justice or judge who speaks my official language` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- My language is not an official language: not covered by subsection (1) (subsection (2) is the one).

-- section 530(2)
#ASSERT `Under section 530(2), may the court grant an order that I be tried before a justice or judge who speaks the official language in which I can best give testimony` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- My language is not English or French; I applied in time: the court may grant the order.
#ASSERT `Under section 530(2), may the court grant an order that I be tried before a justice or judge who speaks the official language in which I can best give testimony` FALSE TRUE (Date 2 4 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I applied the day after the appearance: "not later than the time of the appearance".
#ASSERT `Under section 530(2), may the court grant an order that I be tried before a justice or judge who speaks the official language in which I can best give testimony` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I did not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 530(2), may the court grant an order that I be tried before a justice or judge who speaks the official language in which I can best give testimony` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- My language is an official language: not covered by subsection (2).

-- section 530(3)
#ASSERT `Under section 530(3), must the court before which I first appear ensure that I am advised of my right to apply for an order and of the time before which I must apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- This is my first appearance before the justice of the peace.
#ASSERT `Under section 530(3), must the court before which I first appear ensure that I am advised of my right to apply for an order and of the time before which I must apply` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- This is not my first appearance before this court: the subsection speaks of the court "before whom an accused first appears".

-- section 530(4)
#ASSERT `Under section 530(4), may the court by order remand me to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language although I failed to apply` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I did not apply; the court is satisfied it is in the best interests of justice and does not speak my language.
#ASSERT `Under section 530(4), may the court by order remand me to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language although I failed to apply` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I did apply: not covered by subsection (4).
#ASSERT `Under section 530(4), may the court by order remand me to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language although I failed to apply` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The court is not satisfied about the best interests of justice.
#ASSERT `Under section 530(4), may the court by order remand me to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language although I failed to apply` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The court speaks my language already.

-- section 530.01(1)(a)
#ASSERT `Under section 530.01(1)(a), must the prosecutor, on my application, cause the portions of the information or indictment that are not in my language to be translated` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- An order was granted; the prosecutor is a Crown prosecutor; I applied; part of the indictment is in the other official language.
#ASSERT `Under section 530.01(1)(a), must the prosecutor, on my application, cause the portions of the information or indictment that are not in my language to be translated` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- No order has been granted under section 530.
#ASSERT `Under section 530.01(1)(a), must the prosecutor, on my application, cause the portions of the information or indictment that are not in my language to be translated` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The prosecutor is a private prosecutor: "other than a private prosecutor".
#ASSERT `Under section 530.01(1)(a), must the prosecutor, on my application, cause the portions of the information or indictment that are not in my language to be translated` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I did not apply for the translation.
#ASSERT `Under section 530.01(1)(a), must the prosecutor, on my application, cause the portions of the information or indictment that are not in my language to be translated` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- No portion is in the other official language: nothing to translate, and the paragraph does not say what follows.

-- section 530.01(1)(b)
#ASSERT `Under section 530.01(1)(b), must the prosecutor provide me with a written copy of the translated text at the earliest possible time` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The same facts: the prosecutor must give me a written copy of the translated text.
#ASSERT `Under section 530.01(1)(b), must the prosecutor provide me with a written copy of the translated text at the earliest possible time` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- A private prosecutor.
#ASSERT `Under section 530.01(1)(b), must the prosecutor provide me with a written copy of the translated text at the earliest possible time` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- Nothing to translate: whether there is a translated text is for paragraph (a), which does not settle it.

-- section 530.1(a)
#ASSERT `Under section 530.1(a), do I and my counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes during the preliminary inquiry and trial` TRUE `trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- An order was granted; I am at my trial: my counsel and I may use either official language.
#ASSERT `Under section 530.1(a), do I and my counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes during the preliminary inquiry and trial` TRUE `preliminary inquiry` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The same, at the preliminary inquiry.
#ASSERT `Under section 530.1(a), do I and my counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes during the preliminary inquiry and trial` TRUE `sentencing` EQUALS NOTHING   -- At sentencing: the paragraph speaks of the preliminary inquiry and trial.
#ASSERT `Under section 530.1(a), do I and my counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes during the preliminary inquiry and trial` FALSE `trial` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- No order was granted.

-- section 530.1(b)
