#ASSERT `Under section 536(4), must the justice hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge against me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` FALSE FALSE `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I did not elect when put to the election (deemed to have elected a jury).
#ASSERT `Under section 536(4), must the justice hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge against me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I elected trial by a provincial court judge: no preliminary inquiry under this subsection.
#ASSERT `Under section 536(4), must the justice hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge against me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Nobody requested a preliminary inquiry in time.
#ASSERT `Under section 536(4), must the justice hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge against me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- A direct indictment was preferred: "subject to section 577".

-- section 536.1(2)
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- In Nunavut, before a judge; an indictable offence carrying 14 years, not in section 469; the information has been read.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) a justice of the peace` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The same, before a justice of the peace.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) a judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The offence is listed in section 469: "other than an offence mentioned in section 469".
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Only 10 years: that is subsection (2.1), not (2).
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The information has not been read yet: "after the information has been read to the accused".
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) someone who is neither a justice of the peace nor a judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I am before neither a judge nor a justice of the peace.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 0 `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- No maximum stated.

-- section 536.1(2.1)
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2.1), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2.1)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- In Nunavut, before a judge; 10 years; not listed in 553 or 469; the information has been read.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2.1), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2.1)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 14 years: that is subsection (2).
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2.1), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2.1)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 334 "" `s 553(a)(i) theft` FALSE FALSE 100 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Theft of 100 dollars: absolute jurisdiction under section 553.
