#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(2.1), must the judge or justice of the peace put me to an election in the words of subsection (2.1)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The information has not been read.

-- section 536.1(3)
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(3), must the justice or judge hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge against me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- Charged in Nunavut with a 14-year offence; I elected a judge without a jury; a request for a preliminary inquiry was made; no direct indictment.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(3), must the justice or judge hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge against me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE FALSE `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I did not elect when put to the election (deemed to have elected a jury).
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(3), must the justice or judge hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge against me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I elected trial by a provincial court judge: no preliminary inquiry under this subsection.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(3), must the justice or judge hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge against me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Nobody requested a preliminary inquiry in time.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.1(3), must the justice or judge hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge against me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 14 `s 536.1(1) a judge` FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- A direct indictment was preferred: "subject to section 577".

-- section 536.2
#ASSERT `Under section 536.2, may my election or re-election be made by a document in writing without my personal appearance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I am making my election by a document in writing.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.2, may my election or re-election be made by a document in writing without my personal appearance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- It is not an election or re-election by an accused: not covered.

-- section 536.3
#ASSERT `Under section 536.3, must my counsel provide the statement of issues and witnesses for the preliminary inquiry` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I requested the preliminary inquiry and I have counsel.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.3, must my counsel provide the statement of issues and witnesses for the preliminary inquiry` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The prosecutor made the request: the prosecutor provides the statement.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.3, must my counsel provide the statement of issues and witnesses for the preliminary inquiry` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- No request has been made.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.3, must my counsel provide the statement of issues and witnesses for the preliminary inquiry` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I made the request but have no counsel: the text does not say who provides the statement.

-- section 536.5
#ASSERT `Under section 536.5, may the prosecutor and I agree to limit the scope of the preliminary inquiry to specific issues` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- A preliminary inquiry is to be held.
#ASSERT `Under section 536.5, may the prosecutor and I agree to limit the scope of the preliminary inquiry to specific issues` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- No preliminary inquiry is to be held: not covered.

-- section 537(1)(j)
#ASSERT `Under section 537(1)(j), may the justice allow me to appear by counsel for a part of the inquiry` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- At the inquiry, the prosecutor and I consent to my appearing by counsel for a part where no witness gives evidence.
#ASSERT `Under section 537(1)(j), may the justice allow me to appear by counsel for a part of the inquiry` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The part is one in which the evidence of a witness is taken: "other than a part in which the evidence of a witness is taken".
#ASSERT `Under section 537(1)(j), may the justice allow me to appear by counsel for a part of the inquiry` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The prosecutor does not consent.
#ASSERT `Under section 537(1)(j), may the justice allow me to appear by counsel for a part of the inquiry` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The justice is not acting under this Part.

-- section 537(1)(j.1)
#ASSERT `Under section 537(1)(j.1), may the justice permit me to be out of court during the whole or any part of the inquiry` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I asked to be out of court for part of the inquiry.
#ASSERT `Under section 537(1)(j.1), may the justice permit me to be out of court during the whole or any part of the inquiry` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I did not ask.
#ASSERT `Under section 537(1)(j.1), may the justice permit me to be out of court during the whole or any part of the inquiry` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The justice is not acting under this Part.

-- section 537(1.02)
#ASSERT `Under section 537(1.02), must the Court inform me that the evidence taken during my absence could still be admissible under section 715 or 715.01` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The justice granted my request to be out of court.
#ASSERT `Under section 537(1.02), must the Court inform me that the evidence taken during my absence could still be admissible under section 715 or 715.01` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- No such request was granted.

-- section 539(1)(b)
#ASSERT `Under section 539(1)(b), must the justice make an order restricting publication of the evidence taken at my preliminary inquiry if I apply for it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I applied for a publication ban before any evidence was taken.
#ASSERT `Under section 539(1)(b), must the justice make an order restricting publication of the evidence taken at my preliminary inquiry if I apply for it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The application was not made by me or by any of the accused.
#ASSERT `Under section 539(1)(b), must the justice make an order restricting publication of the evidence taken at my preliminary inquiry if I apply for it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Evidence has already begun.

-- section 539(2)
#ASSERT `Under section 539(2), must the justice inform me of my right to apply for an order restricting publication` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I have no counsel and no evidence has been taken yet.
#ASSERT `Under section 539(2), must the justice inform me of my right to apply for an order restricting publication` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I am represented by counsel.
#ASSERT `Under section 539(2), must the justice inform me of my right to apply for an order restricting publication` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The taking of evidence has commenced.

-- section 540(1)(a)
#ASSERT `Under section 540(1)(a), must the justice take the evidence of the prosecution witnesses under oath and allow me or my counsel to cross-examine them` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- At my preliminary inquiry; the justice has not limited the witnesses.
#ASSERT `Under section 540(1)(a), must the justice take the evidence of the prosecution witnesses under oath and allow me or my counsel to cross-examine them` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I am not before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry.
#ASSERT `Under section 540(1)(a), must the justice take the evidence of the prosecution witnesses under oath and allow me or my counsel to cross-examine them` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The justice has limited the witnesses under subsection 537(1.01): "subject to subsection 537(1.01)".

-- section 541(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 541(1), must the justice hear the witnesses I call` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The prosecution witnesses are done; the justice must hear mine.
#ASSERT `Under section 541(1), must the justice hear the witnesses I call` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The prosecution witnesses are not done yet.
#ASSERT `Under section 541(1), must the justice hear the witnesses I call` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The justice has limited the witnesses.

-- section 541(2)
#ASSERT `Under section 541(2), must the justice address me in the words of subsection (2) when I am not represented by counsel` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I have no counsel and the justice has not yet begun to hear my witnesses.
#ASSERT `Under section 541(2), must the justice address me in the words of subsection (2) when I am not represented by counsel` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I am represented by counsel: the subsection speaks of "an accused who is not represented by counsel" (a scope limit, not "only"), so not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 541(2), must the justice address me in the words of subsection (2) when I am not represented by counsel` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The justice has already begun to hear my witness.

-- section 541(4)
#ASSERT `Under section 541(4), must the justice ask me whether I wish to call any witnesses when I am not represented by counsel` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I have no counsel; subsections (2) and (3) have been complied with.
#ASSERT `Under section 541(4), must the justice ask me whether I wish to call any witnesses when I am not represented by counsel` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I am represented by counsel.
#ASSERT `Under section 541(4), must the justice ask me whether I wish to call any witnesses when I am not represented by counsel` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The address under subsection (2) has not yet been made.

-- section 544(1)(a)
#ASSERT `Under section 544(1)(a), am I deemed to have waived the right to be present at the inquiry because I absconded` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I ran away during my preliminary inquiry.
#ASSERT `Under section 544(1)(a), am I deemed to have waived the right to be present at the inquiry because I absconded` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I did not abscond.

-- section 544(2)
#ASSERT `Under section 544(2), may the justice draw an inference adverse to me from the fact that I absconded` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The justice continued the inquiry in my absence.
#ASSERT `Under section 544(2), may the justice draw an inference adverse to me from the fact that I absconded` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The justice did not continue the inquiry (listed: where/when/upon group).

-- section 544(3)
#ASSERT `Under section 544(3), am I not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in my absence re-opened when I reappear at a preliminary inquiry that is continuing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I reappeared at the continuing inquiry and no exceptional circumstances were found: I am not entitled to have the part held in my absence re-opened.
#ASSERT `Under section 544(3), am I not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in my absence re-opened when I reappear at a preliminary inquiry that is continuing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I have not reappeared at a continuing inquiry: "Where an accused reappears".
#ASSERT `Under section 544(3), am I not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in my absence re-opened when I reappear at a preliminary inquiry that is continuing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The justice is satisfied that exceptional circumstances make it in the interests of justice to re-open: "unless the justice is satisfied".

-- section 544(5)
#ASSERT `Under section 544(5), must my counsel be given an opportunity to call witnesses on my behalf although I am absent` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The prosecution evidence concluded; I am absent; my counsel is present.
#ASSERT `Under section 544(5), must my counsel be given an opportunity to call witnesses on my behalf although I am absent` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I am present: the subsection speaks of an absent accused.
#ASSERT `Under section 544(5), must my counsel be given an opportunity to call witnesses on my behalf although I am absent` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- My counsel is not present.
#ASSERT `Under section 544(5), must my counsel be given an opportunity to call witnesses on my behalf although I am absent` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The justice has limited the witnesses.

-- section 548
#ASSERT `Under section 548, what decision does the justice make at my preliminary inquiry` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `an order to stand trial`   -- All the evidence has been taken; the justice finds sufficient evidence.
#ASSERT `Under section 548, what decision does the justice make at my preliminary inquiry` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `a discharge at the preliminary inquiry`   -- All the evidence has been taken; the justice finds the evidence insufficient.
#ASSERT `Under section 548, what decision does the justice make at my preliminary inquiry` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The evidence is not all in: the section speaks of "When all the evidence has been taken".

-- section 548(1)(a)
#ASSERT `Under section 548(1)(a), must the justice order me to stand trial` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The evidence is sufficient: the justice must order me to stand trial.
#ASSERT `Under section 548(1)(a), must the justice order me to stand trial` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The evidence is not sufficient.
#ASSERT `Under section 548(1)(a), must the justice order me to stand trial` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The evidence is not all in.

-- section 548(1)(b)
#ASSERT `Under section 548(1)(b), must the justice discharge me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The evidence is not sufficient: the justice must discharge me.
#ASSERT `Under section 548(1)(b), must the justice discharge me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The evidence is sufficient.
#ASSERT `Under section 548(1)(b), must the justice discharge me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The evidence is not all in.

-- section 549(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 549(1), may the justice order me to stand trial without taking or recording any evidence or further evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The prosecutor and I both consent to my being ordered to stand trial without more evidence.
#ASSERT `Under section 549(1), may the justice order me to stand trial without taking or recording any evidence or further evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The prosecutor does not consent: outside the grant.
#ASSERT `Under section 549(1), may the justice order me to stand trial without taking or recording any evidence or further evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I do not consent.

-- section 551.1(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 551.1(1), may the Chief Justice or Chief Judge appoint a judge as the case management judge for my trial` TRUE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- A jury trial is to be held; the Chief Justice thinks a case management judge is needed; jury selection has not begun.
#ASSERT `Under section 551.1(1), may the Chief Justice or Chief Judge appoint a judge as the case management judge for my trial` TRUE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Jury selection has begun: "at any time before the jury selection".
#ASSERT `Under section 551.1(1), may the Chief Justice or Chief Judge appoint a judge as the case management judge for my trial` TRUE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- A trial without a jury, and the evidence on the merits is already being presented.
#ASSERT `Under section 551.1(1), may the Chief Justice or Chief Judge appoint a judge as the case management judge for my trial` TRUE FALSE `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The Chief Justice is not of that opinion: outside the grant.
#ASSERT `Under section 551.1(1), may the Chief Justice or Chief Judge appoint a judge as the case management judge for my trial` FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- No trial is to be held before the court.

-- section 551.5
#ASSERT `Under section 551.5, must my trial proceed continuously` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The trial has not been adjourned: it proceeds continuously.
#ASSERT `Under section 551.5, must my trial proceed continuously` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The court has adjourned the trial: "subject to adjournment by the court".

-- section 553
#ASSERT `Under section 553, is the offence I am charged with within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` TRUE 334 "" `s 553(a)(i) theft` FALSE FALSE 100 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- Charged in an information with theft of 100 dollars.
#ASSERT `Under section 553, is the offence I am charged with within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` TRUE 334 "" `s 553(a)(i) theft` FALSE FALSE 9000 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Theft of 9,000 dollars: over 5,000.
#ASSERT `Under section 553, is the offence I am charged with within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` FALSE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Not charged in an information.
#ASSERT `Under section 553, is the offence I am charged with within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- An offence that section 553 does not name.

-- section 554(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 554(1), may a provincial court judge try me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- Indictable offence, not in 469, not absolute; I elected trial by a provincial court judge; not Nunavut.
#ASSERT `Under section 554(1), may a provincial court judge try me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I elected a judge without a jury: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 554(1), may a provincial court judge try me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The offence is listed in section 469: outside the grant.
#ASSERT `Under section 554(1), may a provincial court judge try me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 334 "" `s 553(a)(i) theft` FALSE FALSE 100 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- Theft of 100 dollars: absolute jurisdiction (section 553).
#ASSERT `Under section 554(1), may a provincial court judge try me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The proceedings are in Nunavut: "Subject to subsection (2)".
#ASSERT `Under section 554(1), may a provincial court judge try me` `an offence punishable on summary conviction` `on summary conviction` FALSE 2 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- A summary conviction offence.

-- section 554(2)
#ASSERT `Under section 554(2), may a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice try me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- In Nunavut, indictable offence, not in 469, not absolute; I elected a judge without a jury.
#ASSERT `Under section 554(2), may a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice try me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The proceedings are not in Nunavut.
#ASSERT `Under section 554(2), may a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice try me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I elected a provincial court judge.
#ASSERT `Under section 554(2), may a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice try me` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE 267 "" `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` FALSE FALSE 0 `s 553(b) with the offence itself` FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The offence is listed in section 469.

-- section 555(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 555(1), may the provincial court judge decide not to adjudicate` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- Before the provincial court judge, who thinks the charge should be prosecuted by indictment; I have not entered a defence.
#ASSERT `Under section 555(1), may the provincial court judge decide not to adjudicate` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I have entered a defence: "at any time before the accused has entered a defence".
#ASSERT `Under section 555(1), may the provincial court judge decide not to adjudicate` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I am not before a provincial court judge in Part XIX proceedings.

-- section 555.1(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 555.1(1), may the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice decide not to adjudicate` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- Before a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice, who thinks the charge should be prosecuted by indictment; I have not entered a defence.
#ASSERT `Under section 555.1(1), may the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice decide not to adjudicate` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I have entered a defence: "at any time before the accused has entered a defence".
#ASSERT `Under section 555.1(1), may the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice decide not to adjudicate` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I am not before a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice in Part XIX proceedings.
#ASSERT `Under section 555.1(1), may the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice decide not to adjudicate` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- It does not appear that the charge should be prosecuted by indictment.

-- section 555(1)
