#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), where the Attorney General requires me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536.1(3)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- A preliminary inquiry has already been held: "unless one has already been held".
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), where the Attorney General requires me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536.1(3)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- My re-election was made under subsection 565(2).
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), where the Attorney General requires me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536.1(3)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I did not request a preliminary inquiry.
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), where the Attorney General requires me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536.1(3)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The Attorney General has not required a jury.
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), where the Attorney General requires me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536.1(3)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The offence carries 5 years: the Attorney General could not so require.

-- section 569(1)c
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), if the Attorney General requires a jury, is a judge without jurisdiction to try me under Part XIX` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The Attorney General requires a jury for my 10-year offence: the judge has no jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), if the Attorney General requires a jury, is a judge without jurisdiction to try me under Part XIX` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The Attorney General has not required it.
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), if the Attorney General requires a jury, is a judge without jurisdiction to try me under Part XIX` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 5 TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- A 5-year offence: not "so" required.

-- section 569(1)a
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- In Nunavut; the offence carries 10 years; I elected a judge without a jury: the Attorney General may require a jury.
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 5 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The offence carries 5 years: "unless the alleged offence is one that is punishable with imprisonment for five years or less".
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 6 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The offence carries 6 years.
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I did not elect a judge without a jury: the section speaks of an accused who so elects.
#ASSERT `Under section 569(1), may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The section creating the offence states no maximum: not covered.

-- section 568a
#ASSERT `Under section 568, may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The offence carries 10 years; I elected a judge: the Attorney General may require a jury.
#ASSERT `Under section 568, may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 5 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The offence carries 5 years: "unless the alleged offence is one that is punishable with imprisonment for five years or less".
#ASSERT `Under section 568, may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 6 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The offence carries 6 years.
#ASSERT `Under section 568, may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` TRUE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The offence carries life imprisonment.
#ASSERT `Under section 568, may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- I did not elect a judge or provincial court judge.
#ASSERT `Under section 568, may the Attorney General require me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- No maximum stated.

-- section 568b
#ASSERT `Under section 568, where the Attorney General requires me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536(4)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The Attorney General requires a jury; I request a preliminary inquiry; none was held; not a section 565(2) re-election. -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 568, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536(4)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question was retitled to the route its body answers, the answer is unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 568, where the Attorney General requires me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536(4)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- A preliminary inquiry has already been held: "unless one has already been held". -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 568, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536(4)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the question was retitled to the route its body answers, the answer is unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 568, where the Attorney General requires me to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536(4)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- My re-election was made under subsection 565(2). -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 568, must a preliminary inquiry be held if I request one under subsection 536(4)` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the question was retitled to the route its body answers, the answer is unchanged
