-- section 568c
#ASSERT `Under section 568, if the Attorney General requires a jury, is a judge or provincial court judge without jurisdiction to try me under Part XIX` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The Attorney General requires a jury for my 10-year offence: the judge has no jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Under section 568, if the Attorney General requires a jury, is a judge or provincial court judge without jurisdiction to try me under Part XIX` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 10 TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The Attorney General has not required it.
#ASSERT `Under section 568, if the Attorney General requires a jury, is a judge or provincial court judge without jurisdiction to try me under Part XIX` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` FALSE 5 TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- A 5-year offence: not "so" required.

-- section 570(1)a
#ASSERT `Under section 570(1), must the judge or provincial court judge sentence me or otherwise deal with me in the manner authorized by law once I am determined to be guilty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I pleaded guilty and was determined to be guilty.
#ASSERT `Under section 570(1), must the judge or provincial court judge sentence me or otherwise deal with me in the manner authorized by law once I am determined to be guilty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I was not determined to be guilty.

-- section 570(1)b
#ASSERT `Under section 570(1), must a conviction in Form 35 and a certified copy of it, or an order in Form 36 and a certified copy of it, be drawn up on request` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I was found guilty; my counsel asked for a conviction and certified copy.
#ASSERT `Under section 570(1), must a conviction in Form 35 and a certified copy of it, or an order in Form 36 and a certified copy of it, be drawn up on request` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Nobody has asked.
#ASSERT `Under section 570(1), must a conviction in Form 35 and a certified copy of it, or an order in Form 36 and a certified copy of it, be drawn up on request` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I was not found guilty.

-- section 570(2)a
#ASSERT `Under section 570(2), must the judge or provincial court judge immediately acquit me when I am found not guilty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I was found not guilty.
#ASSERT `Under section 570(2), must the judge or provincial court judge immediately acquit me when I am found not guilty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I was not found not guilty.

-- section 570(2)b
#ASSERT `Under section 570(2), must a certified copy of the order of acquittal be drawn up and delivered to me on request` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I was found not guilty and I asked for a certified copy of the order.
#ASSERT `Under section 570(2), must a certified copy of the order of acquittal be drawn up and delivered to me on request` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I did not ask.

-- section 570(4)
#ASSERT `Under section 570(4), is a copy of a conviction or order sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- A certified copy of a conviction; the person's identity is proved.
#ASSERT `Under section 570(4), is a copy of a conviction or order sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The identity is not proved: "on proof of the identity".
#ASSERT `Under section 570(4), is a copy of a conviction or order sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The copy is not certified or proved true: the subsection says nothing of it.
#ASSERT `Under section 570(4), is a copy of a conviction or order sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- It is not a copy of a conviction or an order in those Forms.

-- section 570(5)
#ASSERT `Under section 570(5), must the judge or provincial court judge issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 when I am convicted` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- I am an individual and I am convicted: the judge must issue a warrant of committal in Form 21.
#ASSERT `Under section 570(5), must the judge or provincial court judge issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 when I am convicted` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The accused is an organization: "other than an organization".
#ASSERT `Under section 570(5), must the judge or provincial court judge issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 when I am convicted` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- I am not convicted.

-- section 571(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 571(1), may a judge or provincial court judge acting under Part XIX adjourn my trial from time to time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The trial is not finished: the judge may adjourn it from time to time.
#ASSERT `Under section 571(1), may a judge or provincial court judge acting under Part XIX adjourn my trial from time to time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- The trial is finally terminated: "until it is finally terminated" (listed: where/when/upon group).
#ASSERT `Under section 571(1), may a judge or provincial court judge acting under Part XIX adjourn my trial from time to time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The judge is not acting under Part XIX.

-- section 571(2)
#ASSERT `Under section 571(2), must the judge or provincial court judge consider the interests of justice in deciding whether to adjourn my trial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The judge is deciding whether to adjourn: must consider the interests of justice.
#ASSERT `Under section 571(2), must the judge or provincial court judge consider the interests of justice in deciding whether to adjourn my trial` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- No adjournment is being decided.

-- section 572
#ASSERT `Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, a provision of Part XVIII about the transmission of the record by a provincial court judge who holds a preliminary inquiry, or a provision of Part XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me` 551 "" TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- The provision is section 551 (transmission of the record). -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, XVIII, XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me` 551 "" TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question was retitled to the route its body answers, the answer is unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, a provision of Part XVIII about the transmission of the record by a provincial court judge who holds a preliminary inquiry, or a provision of Part XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me` 551 "" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The provision is in Part XVIII and is not about transmission of the record. -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, XVIII, XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me` 551 "" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the question was retitled to the route its body answers, the answer is unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, a provision of Part XVIII about the transmission of the record by a provincial court judge who holds a preliminary inquiry, or a provision of Part XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me` 600 "" TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- A Part XX provision that is inconsistent with Part XIX: "in so far as they are not inconsistent". -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, XVIII, XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me` 600 "" TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the question was retitled to the route its body answers, the answer is unchanged
#ASSERT `Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, a provision of Part XVIII about the transmission of the record by a provincial court judge who holds a preliminary inquiry, or a provision of Part XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me` 600 "" FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- The proceedings are not under this Part. -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, XVIII, XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me` 600 "" FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the question was retitled to the route its body answers, the answer is unchanged

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ccc22 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc22-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for ccc22-seat.l4. Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion (the reading is the same as in the layer-1 test file of the section's module, where the same facts are tried). Arguments are in the order of each question's GIVEN lines.
-- Every question has at least two cases: one on which the text gives the answer the question asks, and one on which it gives the opposite answer or says nothing.

§ `Criminal Code (Canada) -- cases for the accused's questions (sections 573 to 672)`

§§ `Part XIX.1 -- the Nunavut Court of Justice (ss 573 to 573.2)`

#ASSERT `Under section 573.1(2), does the section bar review of the decision or order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `Under section 573.1(2), does the section bar review of the decision or order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 573.2(1), may habeas corpus proceedings be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 573.2(1), may habeas corpus proceedings be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "except where (a)"

§§ `Indictments, process and stays (ss 574 to 580)`

#ASSERT `Under section 574(3), does the section bar preferring the indictment without the written order of a judge` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- private prosecution, no intervention, no order: the bar applies
#ASSERT `Under section 574(3), does the section bar preferring the indictment without the written order of a judge` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the written order is there: outside the prohibition
#ASSERT `Under section 576(3), does the section bar trying a person on a coroner’s inquisition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 576(3), does the section bar trying a person on a coroner’s inquisition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 577, has a direct indictment been preferred` TRUE `s 577 the accused has not been given the opportunity to request a preliminary inquiry` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `Under section 577, has a direct indictment been preferred` TRUE `s 577 a preliminary inquiry has been commenced but not concluded` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) is the case, and the personal consent is not filed; the judge's order is for "any other case"
#ASSERT `Under section 578(1), may the court issue a summons or a warrant for my arrest` TRUE FALSE TRUE `a summons` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 578(1), may the court issue a summons or a warrant for my arrest` FALSE FALSE TRUE `a summons` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither notice nor filed indictment: "Where" fails
#ASSERT `Under section 579(1), are the proceedings against me stayed and any undertaking or release order relating to them vacated` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 579(1), are the proceedings against me stayed and any undertaking or release order relating to them vacated` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 579(2), are the proceedings against me deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2030) TRUE (Date 11 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 579(2), are the proceedings against me deemed never to have been commenced` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2030) TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 580, is the indictment sufficient` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 580, is the indictment sufficient` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Counts, particulars and details (ss 581 to 588)`

#ASSERT `Under section 581(3), does the count contain sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 581(3), does the count contain sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 581(3), does the absence or insufficiency of details vitiate the count` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not vitiate the count"
#ASSERT `Under section 581(3), does the absence or insufficiency of details vitiate the count` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "but otherwise": the subsection does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 582, does the section bar a conviction for high treason or first degree murder` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 582, does the section bar a conviction for high treason or first degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless ... he is specifically charged"
#ASSERT `Under section 587(1), may the court order the prosecutor to furnish particulars` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 587(1), may the court order the prosecutor to furnish particulars` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where it is satisfied that it is necessary for a fair trial" (ruling (b): where)

§§ `Joinder of counts and separate trials (ss 589 to 596)`

#ASSERT `Under section 589, does the section bar joining the count to a count that charges murder` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 589, does the section bar joining the count to a count that charges murder` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `Under section 590(2), may I apply to the court to amend or to divide the count` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 590(2), may I apply to the court to amend or to divide the count` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 591(3), may the court order that the accused or counts be tried separately` TRUE FALSE `s 591(3)(a) that the accused or defendant be tried separately on one or more of the counts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 591(3), may the court order that the accused or counts be tried separately` FALSE TRUE `s 591(3)(a) that the accused or defendant be tried separately on one or more of the counts` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where it is satisfied that the interests of justice so require"

§§ `Accused at large; trial in another place (ss 597 to 600)`

#ASSERT `Under section 597(1), may the court issue a warrant in Form 7 for my arrest` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 597(1), may the court issue a warrant in Form 7 for my arrest` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person appears and remains
#ASSERT `Under section 598(1), does the subsection bar trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 598(1), does the subsection bar trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) a legitimate excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 599(1), may the court or judge order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `Under section 599(1), may the court or judge order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither (a) nor (b)

§§ `Objections, amendments and copies (ss 601 to 605)`

#ASSERT `Under section 601(1), may the objection be taken` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- by motion to quash before the plea
#ASSERT `Under section 601(1), may the objection be taken` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the plea: "only by leave of the court"
#ASSERT `Under section 601(2), may the court amend the indictment, count or particular to make it conform to the evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 601(2), may the court amend the indictment, count or particular to make it conform to the evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where there is a variance"
#ASSERT `Under section 603(a), am I entitled to inspect without charge` TRUE `s 603(a) the indictment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 603(a), am I entitled to inspect without charge` FALSE `s 603(a) the indictment` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not yet ordered to stand trial and not at trial
#ASSERT `Under section 603(b), am I entitled to receive a copy` TRUE TRUE `s 603(b)(i) the evidence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 603(b), am I entitled to receive a copy` TRUE FALSE `s 603(b)(i) the evidence` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "on payment of a reasonable fee"
#ASSERT `Under section 603, does the section bar postponing the trial to enable me to secure copies` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- arg: the court is satisfied that the failure is not attributable to lack of diligence
#ASSERT `Under section 603, does the section bar postponing the trial to enable me to secure copies` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless"

§§ `Pleas and special pleas (ss 606 to 619)`

#ASSERT `Under section 606(1), may I enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) not guilty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 606(1), may I enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) some other plea` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "and no others"
#ASSERT `Under section 606(1.1), may the court accept a plea of guilty` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 606(1.1), may the court accept a plea of guilty` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `Under section 606(1.2), does the court’s failure to inquire affect the validity of the plea` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not affect the validity of the plea"
#ASSERT `Under section 606(1.2), does the court’s failure to inquire affect the validity of the plea` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 606(2), must the court order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 606(2), must the court order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 606(3), am I entitled as of right to have the trial postponed` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 606(3), am I entitled as of right to have the trial postponed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 606(4), may the court accept my plea of guilty of the other offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 606(4), may the court accept my plea of guilty of the other offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "with the consent of the prosecutor"
#ASSERT `Under section 607(1), may I plead the special plea` `s 606(1) autrefois acquit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 607(1), may I plead the special plea` `s 606(1) guilty` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 607(6), does the subsection bar the plea of autrefois convict` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 607(6), does the subsection bar the plea of autrefois convict` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) fails: the person was punished
#ASSERT `Under section 609(1), must the judge give judgment discharging me in respect of the count` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 609(1), must the judge give judgment discharging me in respect of the count` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 610(1), does the previous conviction or acquittal bar the subsequent indictment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 610(1), does the previous conviction or acquittal bar the subsequent indictment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 610(2), does the previous conviction or acquittal bar a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `first degree murder` `manslaughter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 610(2), does the previous conviction or acquittal bar a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `first degree murder` `second degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- that is subsection (3)
#ASSERT `Under section 611(1), may I plead justification` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 611(1), may I plead justification` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 612(1), does the section bar inquiring into the truth of the matters charged in the alleged libel` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 612(1), does the section bar inquiring into the truth of the matters charged in the alleged libel` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the absence of a plea of justification"
#ASSERT `Under section 613, may the ground of defence be relied on under the plea of not guilty` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- arg: a special plea is provided for the ground of defence
#ASSERT `Under section 613, may the ground of defence be relied on under the plea of not guilty` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Pre-trial conference and the jury (ss 625.1 to 644)`

#ASSERT `Under section 625.1(1), may the court order a conference between the prosecutor and me or my counsel before the proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 625.1(1), may the court order a conference between the prosecutor and me or my counsel before the proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 625.1(2), must a judge of the court order a conference before the trial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 625.1(2), must a judge of the court order a conference before the trial` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 626(1), is the person qualified to serve as a juror in criminal proceedings in the province` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 626(1), is the person qualified to serve as a juror in criminal proceedings in the province` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 626.1, may the judge before whom I am tried be this judge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 626.1, may the judge before whom I am tried be this judge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 629(1), may the accused or the prosecutor challenge the jury panel` TRUE `s 629(1) partiality on the part of the sheriff or other officer by whom the panel was returned` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 629(1), may the accused or the prosecutor challenge the jury panel` TRUE `s 629(1) some other ground` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "only on the ground"
#ASSERT `Under section 638(1), is the prosecutor or the accused entitled to challenge the juror for cause on the ground` TRUE `s 638(1)(b) the juror is not impartial` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 638(1), is the prosecutor or the accused entitled to challenge the juror for cause on the ground` TRUE `s 638(1)(b) the juror is not impartial` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the ground is not made out
#ASSERT `Under section 640(1), must the judge leave a challenged juror unsworn` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under section 640(1), must the judge determine whether the ground is true and, if satisfied that it is, leave the juror unsworn` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE`; question retitled to the limb the body answers (the second limb only)
#ASSERT `Under section 640(1), must the judge leave a challenged juror unsworn` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under section 640(1), must the judge determine whether the ground is true and, if satisfied that it is, leave the juror unsworn` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING`; question retitled to the limb the body answers (the second limb only)
#ASSERT `Under section 643(3), does the failure to comply affect the validity of a proceeding` 643 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 643(3), does the failure to comply affect the validity of a proceeding` 642 EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 642 is not named
#ASSERT `Under section 644(1), may the judge discharge the juror` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 644(1), may the judge discharge the juror` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 644(2), is the jury deemed to remain properly constituted for all purposes of the trial` TRUE 11 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 644(2), is the jury deemed to remain properly constituted for all purposes of the trial` TRUE 9 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 644(3), may the judge discharge the jurors, continue the trial without a jury and render a verdict` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 644(3), may the judge discharge the jurors, continue the trial without a jury and render a verdict` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "with the consent of the parties"

§§ `The trial (ss 645 to 654)`

#ASSERT `Under section 645(2), may a judge adjourn the trial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 645(2), may a judge adjourn the trial` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an adjournment not within the stated limit is not decided here
#ASSERT `Under section 645(3.1), must the judge consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 645(3.1), must the judge consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the duty is "if information ... is readily available"
#ASSERT `Under section 648(1), does the section bar publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the information` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 648(1), does the section bar publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the information` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the jury retires the period has ended
#ASSERT `Under section 648(2), is the person guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 648(2), is the person guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 648(2), what is the class of offence` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the subsection makes the offence one punishable on summary conviction
#ASSERT (`Under section 648(2), what is the punishment the subsection states`)'s `mode` EQUALS `on summary conviction`   -- the subsection states the mode of prosecution
#ASSERT (`Under section 648(2), what is the punishment the subsection states`)'s `maximum imprisonment` EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated`   -- the subsection states no term of imprisonment
#ASSERT (`Under section 648(2), what is the punishment the subsection states`)'s `maximum fine` EQUALS `no fine is stated`   -- the subsection states no fine
#ASSERT `Under section 650(1), does the accused’s presence meet the requirement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 650(1), does the accused’s presence meet the requirement` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 650(1.1), may the court allow the accused to appear by counsel for the part of the trial` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 650(1.1), may the court allow the accused to appear by counsel for the part of the trial` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than a part in which the evidence of a witness is taken"
#ASSERT `Under section 650(3), am I entitled to make full answer and defence personally or by counsel` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 650(3), am I entitled to make full answer and defence personally or by counsel` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the stated period: "after the close of the case for the prosecution"
#ASSERT `Under section 650.01(1), may I appoint counsel to represent me for any proceedings under this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 650.01(1), may I appoint counsel to represent me for any proceedings under this Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "by filing a designation": other ways are not decided here
#ASSERT `Under section 650.01(3)(a), may I appear by the designated counsel without being present for the part` TRUE `s 650.01(3)(a) some other part of the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 650.01(3)(a), may I appear by the designated counsel without being present for the part` TRUE `s 650.01(3)(a)(i) a part during which oral evidence of a witness is taken` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than (i)"
#ASSERT `Under section 651(1), may the prosecutor address the jury by way of summing up` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 651(1), may the prosecutor address the jury by way of summing up` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "if he does not announce his intention": the "if" gate fails (a grant: NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Under section 651(3), who is entitled to address the jury last` TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 651(3) the accused or their counsel`
#ASSERT `Under section 651(3), who is entitled to address the jury last` FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 651(3) counsel for the prosecution`
#ASSERT `Under section 651(4), must all the accused or their respective counsel address the jury before it is addressed by the prosecutor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 651(4), must all the accused or their respective counsel address the jury before it is addressed by the prosecutor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no witness examined for any of them
#ASSERT `Under section 652(3), must the accused and the judge attend the view` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 652(3), must the accused and the judge attend the view` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 653(1), may the judge take the step` TRUE `s 653(1) adjourn the trial on such terms as justice may require` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 653(1), may the judge take the step` FALSE `s 653(1) adjourn the trial on such terms as justice may require` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b)): "Where the judge is satisfied that the jury is unable to agree" governs the adjournment as well as the discharge
#ASSERT `Under section 653.1, are the rulings made during the trial binding on the parties in any new trial` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 653.1, are the rulings made during the trial binding on the parties in any new trial` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the court is satisfied that it would not be in the interests of justice"
#ASSERT `Under section 654, is the taking of the verdict, or a proceeding incidental to it, invalid` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not invalid by reason only that it is done on Sunday or on a holiday"
#ASSERT `Under section 654, is the taking of the verdict, or a proceeding incidental to it, invalid` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Evidence at trial (ss 655 to 659)`

#ASSERT `Under section 655, may the accused or their counsel admit the fact` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 655, may the accused or their counsel admit the fact` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b)): a summary conviction trial
#ASSERT `Under section 656, is the person presumed to have stolen or unlawfully possessed the valuable mineral` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 656, is the person presumed to have stolen or unlawfully possessed the valuable mineral` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary"
#ASSERT `Under section 657, may the statement be given in evidence against the accused without proof of the signature of the justice` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 657, may the statement be given in evidence against the accused without proof of the signature of the justice` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless it is proved that the justice ... did not sign it"
#ASSERT `Under section 657.1(1), is the affidavit or solemn declaration admissible in evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 657.1(1), is the affidavit or solemn declaration admissible in evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "containing the statements referred to in subsection (2)"
#ASSERT `Under section 657.1(3), does the subsection bar receiving the affidavit or solemn declaration in evidence under subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no copy
#ASSERT `Under section 657.1(3), does the subsection bar receiving the affidavit or solemn declaration in evidence under subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- copy and notice given: the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `Under section 657.2(1), is the evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property admissible against the accused` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 657.2(1), is the evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property admissible against the accused` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate
#ASSERT `Under section 657.3(1), may the evidence of the person as an expert be given by means of a report accompanied by the affidavit or solemn declaration` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 657.3(1), may the evidence of the person as an expert be given by means of a report accompanied by the affidavit or solemn declaration` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the "if" gate fails: the court does not recognize the person (a grant: NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Under section 657.3(3)(c), have the accused or their counsel provided the material not later than the close of the case for the prosecution` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 657.3(3)(c), have the accused or their counsel provided the material not later than the close of the case for the prosecution` TRUE TRUE (Date 11 6 2025) (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 657.3(4)(a), must the court grant an adjournment to the party who requests it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 657.3(4)(a), must the court grant an adjournment to the party who requests it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "at the request of any other party"
#ASSERT `Under section 657.3(6), does the subsection bar the prosecutor from producing the material in evidence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 657.3(6), does the subsection bar the prosecutor from producing the material in evidence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "without the consent of the accused": the prohibition is limited by its own wording
#ASSERT `Under section 658(1), is the testimony of a person as to the date of their birth admissible as evidence of that date` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 658(1), is the testimony of a person as to the date of their birth admissible as evidence of that date` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 658(5), may the jury, judge, justice or provincial court judge infer the age of the child or young person from their appearance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 658(5), may the jury, judge, justice or provincial court judge infer the age of the child or young person from their appearance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "In the absence of other evidence, or by way of corroboration" fails
#ASSERT `Under section 659, is the requirement abrogated` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 659, is the requirement abrogated` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other requirement is not decided here

§§ `Verdicts and previous convictions (ss 660 to 669.3)`

#ASSERT `Under section 660, may I be convicted of the attempt` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 660, may I be convicted of the attempt` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the complete offence is proved: the "where" gate fails (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `Under section 661(1), am I entitled to be acquitted` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "the accused is not entitled to be acquitted"
#ASSERT `Under section 661(1), am I entitled to be acquitted` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 661(1), may the jury convict me of the attempt` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 661(1), may the jury convict me of the attempt` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the judge ... discharges the jury from giving a verdict"
#ASSERT `Under section 661(2), am I liable to be tried again for the offence I was charged with attempting to commit` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not liable to be tried again"
#ASSERT `Under section 661(2), am I liable to be tried again for the offence I was charged with attempting to commit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 662(1)(a), may I be convicted of the included offence that is proved` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 662(1)(a), may I be convicted of the included offence that is proved` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "of an offence so included that is proved"
#ASSERT `Under section 662(1)(b), may I be convicted of an attempt to commit the included offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 662(1)(b), may I be convicted of an attempt to commit the included offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 662(2), may the jury find me not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder` `first degree murder` `s 662(2) second degree murder` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 662(2), may the jury find me not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder` `first degree murder` `s 662(2) first degree murder` EQUALS NOTHING   -- first degree murder is proved: the clause is silent
#ASSERT `Under section 662(3), may the jury find me not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 662(3), may the jury find me not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- murder is proved
#ASSERT `Under section 662(3), may the jury on that count find me guilty of any other offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "shall not on that count find the accused guilty of any other offence"
#ASSERT `Under section 662(3), may the jury on that count find me guilty of any other offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "Subject to subsection (4)"
#ASSERT `Under section 662(4), may the jury find me not guilty of murder or infanticide but guilty of an offence under section 243` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 662(4), may the jury find me not guilty of murder or infanticide but guilty of an offence under section 243` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 662(5), may I be convicted of an offence under section 320.13` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 662(5), may I be convicted of an offence under section 320.13` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the offence charged is proved: the clause is silent ("for greater certainty")
#ASSERT `Under section 662(6), may I be convicted of an offence under that latter paragraph` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 662(6), may I be convicted of an offence under that latter paragraph` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b)); subsection (6) carries no "for greater certainty"
#ASSERT `Under section 663, may the female person be convicted of infanticide` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 663, may the female person be convicted of infanticide` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- both (a) and (b) are established: the section gives no such conviction
#ASSERT `Under section 664, does the section bar the indictment from containing any reference to previous convictions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 664, does the section bar the indictment from containing any reference to previous convictions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 666, may the prosecutor adduce evidence of my previous conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 666, may the prosecutor adduce evidence of my previous conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "before a verdict is returned"
#ASSERT `Under section 667(1)(a), is the certificate evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` TRUE TRUE `s 667(1)(a)(iii) a fingerprint examiner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 667(1)(a), is the certificate evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` TRUE TRUE `s 667(1)(a) some other signer` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if it is signed by (i), (ii) or (iii)"
#ASSERT `Under section 667(2.1), is the similarity of name evidence that the defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate or the copy` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 667(2.1), is the similarity of name evidence that the defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate or the copy` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"
#ASSERT `Under section 667(3), may I require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 667(3), may I require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "with leave of the court": the "if"-kind gate fails (a grant: NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Under section 667(4), does the subsection bar receiving the certificate in evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 667(4), does the subsection bar receiving the certificate in evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `Under section 669.2(1), may the proceedings be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` `s 669.2(1)(a) a judge or provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 669.2(1), may the proceedings be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` `s 669.2(1)(a) a judge or provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the judge neither dies nor is unable to continue: a "where" gate (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `Under section 669.3, does the judge or provincial court judge continue to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 669.3, does the judge or provincial court judge continue to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "until its completion"

§§ `Formal defects in jury process; saving of the powers of the court (ss 670 to 672)`

#ASSERT `Under section 670, does the section bar staying or reversing the judgment on the ground` TRUE `s 670(a) an irregularity in the summoning or empanelling of the jury` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 670, does the section bar staying or reversing the judgment on the ground` FALSE `s 670(a) an irregularity in the summoning or empanelling of the jury` EQUALS NOTHING   -- before verdict: the section speaks of judgment "after verdict on an indictment"
#ASSERT `Under section 671, does the section bar treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` TRUE `s 671 the selection of jurors` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 671, does the section bar treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` FALSE `s 671 the selection of jurors` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no omission
#ASSERT `Under section 672, does the Act leave the power, authority, practice or form unaltered` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 672, does the Act leave the power, authority, practice or form unaltered` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "except where ... expressly altered by or is inconsistent with this Act"

