-- ccc24-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for ccc24-seat.l4. Every expected value is written from the text of the section the question names, beside the assertion,
-- before the run; a case whose facts the text does not answer asserts NOTHING. T = JUST TRUE, F = JUST FALSE, N = NOTHING.


§ `Criminal Code -- appeals, review of a conviction, attending as a witness and giving evidence (sections 673 to 715.27): the questions of a person who is, or may be, accused`

§§ `Appealing a conviction or sentence (Part XXI, sections 673 to 677)`
#ASSERT `Under section 673, is this order or disposition part of my "sentence" for the purposes of the appeal rules` 738 "" FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an order under section 738 (restitution) is within "sentence"
#ASSERT `Under section 673, is this order or disposition part of my "sentence" for the purposes of the appeal rules` 16 "" TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an order under the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act
#ASSERT `Under section 673, is this order or disposition part of my "sentence" for the purposes of the appeal rules` 380 "(1)" FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an order under section 380: the list is not closed, so not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 674, are the proceedings I propose barred as an appeal that Part XXI or Part XXVI does not authorize` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an appeal that neither Part authorizes is barred
#ASSERT `Under section 674, are the proceedings I propose barred as an appeal that Part XXI or Part XXVI does not authorize` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- authorized by Part XXI or XXVI: the bar does not apply
#ASSERT `Under section 674, are the proceedings I propose barred as an appeal that Part XXI or Part XXVI does not authorize` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an appeal about an indictable offence: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(1)(a), may I appeal to the court of appeal against my conviction on this ground` TRUE `s 675(1)(a)(i) a ground that involves a question of law alone` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a question of law alone needs no leave
#ASSERT `Under section 675(1)(a), may I appeal to the court of appeal against my conviction on this ground` TRUE `s 675(1)(a)(ii) a ground that involves a question of fact or a question of mixed law and fact` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- fact or mixed: with leave of the court of appeal
#ASSERT `Under section 675(1)(a), may I appeal to the court of appeal against my conviction on this ground` TRUE `s 675(1)(a)(ii) a ground that involves a question of fact or a question of mixed law and fact` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- fact or mixed, without leave or certificate: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(1)(a), may I appeal to the court of appeal against my conviction on this ground` FALSE `s 675(1)(a)(i) a ground that involves a question of law alone` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not convicted by a trial court in proceedings by indictment
#ASSERT `Under section 675(1)(b), may I appeal to the court of appeal against my sentence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- leave granted, sentence not fixed by law
#ASSERT `Under section 675(1)(b), may I appeal to the court of appeal against my sentence` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no leave: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(1)(b), may I appeal to the court of appeal against my sentence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a sentence fixed by law needs no leave ("unless that sentence is one fixed by law")
#ASSERT `Under section 675(1.1), may I appeal my summary conviction or its sentence to the court of appeal as if it had been a conviction by indictment` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- leave granted, tried with an indictable offence that is under appeal
#ASSERT `Under section 675(1.1), may I appeal my summary conviction or its sentence to the court of appeal as if it had been a conviction by indictment` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no appeal of the indictable offence: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2), may I appeal against the number of years beyond ten without eligibility for parole that I was given` `first degree murder` FALSE TRUE 25 EQUALS NOTHING   -- first degree murder is not a kind the subsection names: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2), may I appeal against the number of years beyond ten without eligibility for parole that I was given` `second degree murder` FALSE TRUE 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- second degree murder: 15 years specified is five years in excess of ten
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2), may I appeal against the number of years beyond ten without eligibility for parole that I was given` `manslaughter` TRUE TRUE 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- manslaughter in the paragraph 236(2) circumstances
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2), may I appeal against the number of years beyond ten without eligibility for parole that I was given` `manslaughter` FALSE TRUE 12 EQUALS NOTHING   -- manslaughter outside those circumstances: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2.1), may I appeal to the court of appeal against an order delaying my eligibility for parole` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the order was made against me
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2.1), may I appeal to the court of appeal against an order delaying my eligibility for parole` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no such order was made against me: the subsection is for a person against whom one has been made, so not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2.2), if I was under 18 when I did it, may I appeal against the years beyond the minimum that I must serve before parole` TRUE `second degree murder` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a youth sentenced to a specified period above the minimum
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2.2), if I was under 18 when I did it, may I appeal against the years beyond the minimum that I must serve before parole` FALSE `second degree murder` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not under 18 when the offence was committed: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2.3), may I appeal to the court of appeal against an order of the court under subsection 745.51(1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the order was made against me
#ASSERT `Under section 675(2.3), may I appeal to the court of appeal against an order of the court under subsection 745.51(1)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no such order was made against me: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(3), may I appeal against a verdict that I am unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible` `a verdict of unfit to stand trial` `s 675(1)(a)(i) a ground that involves a question of law alone` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a question of law alone
#ASSERT `Under section 675(3), may I appeal against a verdict that I am unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible` `an acquittal` `s 675(1)(a)(i) a ground that involves a question of law alone` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a verdict the subsection does not name: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 675(4), may I have the court of appeal decide my application for leave to appeal after a judge refused it` TRUE FALSE TRUE 7 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- filed on the seventh day
#ASSERT `Under section 675(4), may I have the court of appeal decide my application for leave to appeal after a judge refused it` TRUE FALSE TRUE 8 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- eight days is outside the seven the subsection fixes
#ASSERT `Under section 675(4), may I have the court of appeal decide my application for leave to appeal after a judge refused it` TRUE TRUE TRUE 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a refusal under paragraph 675(1)(b) is outside "otherwise than under paragraph (1)(b)"
#ASSERT `Under section 675(4), may I have the court of appeal decide my application for leave to appeal after a judge refused it` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where a judge of the court of appeal refuses leave": no refusal
#ASSERT `Under section 676(1)(a), may the Attorney General appeal against my acquittal or my verdict of not criminally responsible` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the Attorney General appeals an acquittal on a question of law
#ASSERT `Under section 676(1)(a), may the Attorney General appeal against my acquittal or my verdict of not criminally responsible` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a ground that is not law alone: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 676(1)(b), may the Attorney General appeal against an order of a superior court that quashed my indictment or refused to exercise jurisdiction on it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 676(1)(b), may the Attorney General appeal against an order of a superior court that quashed my indictment or refused to exercise jurisdiction on it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another kind of order: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 676(1)(c), may the Attorney General appeal against an order of the trial court that stayed my proceedings or quashed my indictment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 676(1)(c), may the Attorney General appeal against an order of the trial court that stayed my proceedings or quashed my indictment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the Attorney General
#ASSERT `Under section 676(1)(d), may the Attorney General appeal against my sentence` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- leave granted, sentence not fixed by law
