-- ccc28-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for the seat layer ccc28-seat.l4. Each case states the facts a real person in the seat would state and asserts the answer.
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the section, beside each assertion; they were never copied from the encoding's output.
-- Every case file ends with assertions written equal to assertions satisfied (the count is printed by check.sh).


§ `Part XXIV: dangerous offenders and long-term offenders`

