#ASSERT `Under section 784(5), does an appeal lie at the instance of this appellant from the judgment on the return of a writ of habeas corpus` TRUE `s 784(5) an appeal from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` `s 784(5) the applicant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- to the Supreme Court of Canada without leave: the appeal lies 'with the leave of that Court'
#ASSERT `Under section 784(5), does an appeal lie at the instance of this appellant from the judgment on the return of a writ of habeas corpus` TRUE `s 784(5) an appeal from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` `s 784(5) the applicant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- with leave

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ccc29 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc29-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for the seat questions of ccc29-seat.l4: the facts a person who is, or may be, accused would state, and the answer the text gives.
-- Every expected value is decided from the text of the section before the run (the text of each section is quoted in the layer-1 module that the question calls) and written beside its case.
-- JUST TRUE is a yes the text gives; JUST FALSE is a no the text gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not answer on these facts".

