-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ccc30 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc30-cases-seat.l4 -- the cases for the seat layer (ccc30-seat.l4): Forms 1 to 23 of the Criminal Code (Canada), asked by the person who is, or may be, accused.
-- Each case states the facts a real person in the seat would state and the answer the TEXT of the Form gives, written by hand before the run; the layer-1 modules have
-- their own tests (ccc30-tests-forms-*.l4). JUST TRUE: the Form says so. JUST FALSE: the Form's own no. NOTHING: not covered, never "no".
-- The people in the cases (Amara, Ben, Chen, Dana, Eli, Farah, Gus, Hana) are invented for these tests; none is a real person.

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      ss IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Provision of the Code`
`forms 1 to 23 cases provision` MEANS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS n, `subsection` IS ss

§ `Cases -- Search warrants and the information (Forms 2, 4 and 5.1)`

-- Amara is charged by an information. Her lawyer asks whether her date of birth may be put on it (Form 2 Note).
#ASSERT `Under form 2, may the date of birth of the accused be mentioned on this document` `an information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Amara is later tried on an indictment: the Note names it too.
#ASSERT `Under form 2, may the date of birth of the accused be mentioned on this document` `an indictment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The document is a summons: the Note does not speak to it.
#ASSERT `Under form 2, may the date of birth of the accused be mentioned on this document` `a summons` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Ben's flat was searched. The officers seized his laptop (Form 5.1: the things seized may be brought before the court).
#ASSERT `Under form 5.1, may the things seized in the search of my premises be brought before the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Nothing was seized from Chen's flat: the "If anything is seized" sentence does not apply.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 5.1, may the things seized in the search of my premises be brought before the court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `Under form 5.1, may the things seized in the search of my premises be brought before the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A report was filed with the court, so Ben may ask the clerk for a copy.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.1, may I obtain a copy of the report on the things that were seized from the clerk of the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No report was filed: the sentence's "if" is unmet.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 5.1, may I obtain a copy of the report on the things that were seized from the clerk of the court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `Under form 5.1, may I obtain a copy of the report on the things that were seized from the clerk of the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Cases -- A demand or order served on you for computer data, an account or documents (Forms 5.001 to 5.0091)`

-- Dana runs a small web-hosting company and was served with a preservation demand that says "until 22 January 2026". On 20 January the data was hers to keep, the demand stood.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.001, am I still required to preserve the computer data` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On 22 January itself (the date read as the last day of the duty): still required.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.001, am I still required to preserve the computer data` TRUE (Date 22 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On 23 January: the date has passed.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.001, am I still required to preserve the computer data` TRUE (Date 23 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The demand was revoked on 15 January: "unless, before that date, this demand is revoked".
#ASSERT `Under form 5.001, am I still required to preserve the computer data` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Dana deleted the data and has no lawful excuse: the demand says a fine; it names no imprisonment for contravening the demand itself.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.001, may I be subject to a fine or to imprisonment for contravening the preservation demand` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 5.001, may I be subject to a fine or to imprisonment for contravening the preservation demand` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 imprisonment` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Dana had a lawful excuse (the server failed): the words "without lawful excuse" limit the sentence; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.001, may I be subject to a fine or to imprisonment for contravening the preservation demand` TRUE TRUE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Dana kept everything: the "If you contravene" is unmet.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.001, may I be subject to a fine or to imprisonment for contravening the preservation demand` FALSE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The information asked for a preservation order for 90 days after the day the order is made; it was made on 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.002, what is the last day of the 90 days for which the information asks me to preserve the data` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 1 4 2026

-- Dana is served with a preservation order until 22 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.003, am I still required to preserve the specified computer data` TRUE (Date 21 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 5.003, am I still required to preserve the specified computer data` TRUE (Date 21 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Contravening the order without lawful excuse: a fine, imprisonment or both.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.003, may I be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both for contravening the preservation order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 5.003, may I be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both for contravening the preservation order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Eli's bank was ordered to keep an account open until 28 February 2026. On 1 March the date has passed.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.0032, am I still required to keep the specified account open or active` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 5.0032, am I still required to keep the specified account open or active` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The account holder asked to close it on 10 February: "unless the holder of the account requests that you close or deactivate it".
#ASSERT `Under form 5.0032, am I still required to keep the specified account open or active` (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Farah was ordered to produce documents within 30 days, at the police station, on paper. She took 30 days: in time.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.005, did I produce the document as the production order requires` 30 30 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- She took 31 days.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.005, did I produce the document as the production order requires` 30 31 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The order is addressed to Farah, so she has the right to apply to revoke or vary it; a person it is not addressed to is not covered.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.005, do I have the right to apply to revoke or vary the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 5.005, do I have the right to apply to revoke or vary the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Gus has not been served with the order to trace a communication: "on being served ... you are ordered".
#ASSERT `Under form 5.006, am I ordered to prepare and produce the document` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under form 5.006, am I ordered to prepare and produce the document` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A non-disclosure order was made on 1 January 2026 for 30 days after: on 15 January Gus may not disclose; on 1 February he may.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.0091, am I prohibited from disclosing the existence of the demand or order on this day` (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 5.0091, am I prohibited from disclosing the existence of the demand or order on this day` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Cases -- Taking of bodily substances for DNA analysis (Forms 5.03, 5.041 and 5.061)`

-- Hana was ordered to give DNA samples. A nurse trained to take them, and not a peace officer, takes the samples under a peace officer's direction, no more than needed.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 5.03, may this person take the samples of bodily substances from me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE`; the question said "may this person take" (a general permission) while the function answers whether THE ORDER authorizes the person (form 5.03 the order authorizes the person to take the samples).
#ASSERT `Under form 5.03, does the order authorize this person to take the samples of bodily substances from me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A friend of the officer with no training takes them: "provided that the person taking the samples is able".
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 5.03, may this person take the samples of bodily substances from me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the question said "may this person take" (a general permission) while the function answers whether THE ORDER authorizes the person (form 5.03 the order authorizes the person to take the samples).
#ASSERT `Under form 5.03, does the order authorize this person to take the samples of bodily substances from me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Someone untrained and not under direction: also no.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 5.03, may this person take the samples of bodily substances from me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the question said "may this person take" (a general permission) while the function answers whether THE ORDER authorizes the person (form 5.03 the order authorizes the person to take the samples).
#ASSERT `Under form 5.03, does the order authorize this person to take the samples of bodily substances from me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- More samples than reasonably required were taken: outside the order's words, not an express no.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 5.03, may this person take the samples of bodily substances from me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; the question said "may this person take" (a general permission) while the function answers whether THE ORDER authorizes the person (form 5.03 the order authorizes the person to take the samples).
#ASSERT `Under form 5.03, does the order authorize this person to take the samples of bodily substances from me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Hana did not turn up on the day: a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for her arrest (order under subsection 487.051(4)).
#ASSERT `Under form 5.041, if I fail to appear as ordered, may a justice of the peace issue a warrant for my arrest` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- She did turn up.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 5.041, if I fail to appear as ordered, may a justice of the peace issue a warrant for my arrest` FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `Under form 5.041, if I fail to appear as ordered, may a justice of the peace issue a warrant for my arrest` FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The instrument is a National Defence Act order: not among those the sentence names.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.041, if I fail to appear as ordered, may a justice of the peace issue a warrant for my arrest` TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Failing to comply with the order, with no reasonable excuse: guilty; with a reasonable excuse (she was in hospital): not covered.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.041, am I guilty of an offence if I fail to comply without reasonable excuse` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 5.041, am I guilty of an offence if I fail to comply without reasonable excuse` TRUE TRUE `forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The most imprisonment the Form quotes on indictment: two years (the quoted limb "(a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years").
#ASSERT `Under form 5.041, what is the most imprisonment I can face on indictment for failing to comply without reasonable excuse` EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE)
-- The summons says the officer may use as much force as necessary to take the samples.
#ASSERT `Under form 5.061, may the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, use the force they used to take the samples from me` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 5.061, may the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, use the force they used to take the samples from me` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Cases -- A summons, an appearance notice, an undertaking or a release order (Forms 6, 9, 10, 11, 11.1 and 12)`

-- Ben was summoned on Form 6 and did not go to court; he has no lawful excuse: the summons warns it is an offence under subsection 145(3).
#ASSERT `Under form 6, am I warned that failing to appear or to attend court, without a lawful excuse, is an offence under subsection 145(3)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- His car broke down on the way to a hearing he could not reschedule: he says it is a lawful excuse ("unless you have a lawful excuse").
#ASSERT `Under form 6, am I warned that failing to appear or to attend court, without a lawful excuse, is an offence under subsection 145(3)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Chen went to court: the warning is about failing; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under form 6, am I warned that failing to appear or to attend court, without a lawful excuse, is an offence under subsection 145(3)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Ben was later charged with a new offence after the summons was issued: the summons may be cancelled.
#ASSERT `Under form 6, may my summons be cancelled` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 6, may my summons be cancelled` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `Under form 6, may my summons be cancelled` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- It was cancelled: he may be detained in custody as a result; if it was not cancelled that result clause does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under form 6, may I be detained in custody as a result of my summons being cancelled` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 6, may I be detained in custody as a result of my summons being cancelled` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Amara's appearance notice describes the offence wrongly; she did not go to court and says that is her excuse: "It is not a lawful excuse".
#ASSERT `Under form 9, is it a lawful excuse that the appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence I am alleged to have committed` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Her excuse is something else (illness): the sentence does not address it.
#ASSERT `Under form 9, is it a lawful excuse that the appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence I am alleged to have committed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No charges were laid, and Amara missed her judicial referral hearing: charges may be laid.
#ASSERT `Under form 9, if no charges have been laid and I fail to appear at a judicial referral hearing, may charges be laid against me for the alleged offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Charges had already been laid: item 6(b) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under form 9, if no charges have been laid and I fail to appear at a judicial referral hearing, may charges be laid against me for the alleged offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under form 9, may my appearance notice be cancelled` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 9, may my appearance notice be cancelled` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `Under form 9, may my appearance notice be cancelled` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Chen is offered an undertaking. A condition that he not contact his former employer is reasonable and needed for the safety of a witness: it may be checked.
#ASSERT `Under form 10, may the peace officer check this condition on my undertaking` TRUE `form 10 to ensure the safety and security of a witness to the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A condition that he stay at home all day, reasonable but not needed for any of the five purposes: "check only those that are ... necessary".
#ASSERT `Under form 10, may the peace officer check this condition on my undertaking` TRUE `form 10 none of those purposes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The officer asks him to promise $500 (the limit), then $750.
#ASSERT `Under form 10, is the amount I am asked to promise to pay within the limit` 500 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 10, is the amount I am asked to promise to pay within the limit` 750 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Chen lives in the province and 40 km away from the station: no deposit may be required on that ground. If he lived 400 km away, one could (up to $500).
#ASSERT `Under form 10, may I be required to deposit money or other valuable security` 300 TRUE 40 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under form 10, may I be required to deposit money or other valuable security` 300 TRUE 400 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 10, may I be required to deposit money or other valuable security` 600 FALSE 400 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Variation: the prosecutor agrees in writing and so does Chen.
#ASSERT `Under form 10, may the conditions of my undertaking be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and myself` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 10, may the conditions of my undertaking be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and myself` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Duration: the conditions stand until cancelled, changed, or he is discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained.
#ASSERT `Under form 10, do the conditions of my undertaking remain in effect` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 10, do the conditions of my undertaking remain in effect` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- He broke a condition with no lawful excuse: an offence under section 145 (what the Form says).
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 10, is failing to follow a condition of my undertaking an offence under section 145` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE`; the question claimed the offence itself while the function answers what the Form's WARNING says (form 10 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, ...).
#ASSERT `Under form 10, does the Form warn that failing to follow a condition of my undertaking, without a lawful excuse, is an offence under section 145` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 10, is failing to follow a condition of my undertaking an offence under section 145` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the question claimed the offence itself while the function answers what the Form's WARNING says (form 10 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, ...).
#ASSERT `Under form 10, does the Form warn that failing to follow a condition of my undertaking, without a lawful excuse, is an offence under section 145` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The promised money could be forfeited if he does not comply.
#ASSERT `Under form 10, could the funds or valuable security promised or deposited be forfeited` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- He does not have to accept the conditions; if he does not, he will be brought to a justice for a bail hearing.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 10, do I have to accept the conditions of the undertaking` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE`; direction: the function answers `the person does not have to accept the conditions`, so JUST TRUE meant "you need not accept", the opposite of how "do I have to accept" reads.
#ASSERT `Under form 10, does the Form say that I do not have to accept the conditions of the undertaking` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 10, if I do not accept the conditions, will I be brought to a justice for a bail hearing` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 10, if I do not accept the conditions, will I be brought to a justice for a bail hearing` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Dana is released on a release order with a surety. She has complied with the money obligations: the Form says what is needed, not what is enough.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 11, will I be released once I have complied with the obligations marked on the release order` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; subject: the question asked whether compliance is enough ("will I be released once ...") while the function states what is NECESSARY (form 11 item 4 the person is released: not complied is JUST FALSE, complied is NOTHING).
#ASSERT `Under form 11, am I released, given whether I have complied with the obligations marked on the release order` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `Under form 11, will I be released once I have complied with the obligations marked on the release order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; subject: the question asked whether compliance is enough ("will I be released once ...") while the function states what is NECESSARY (form 11 item 4 the person is released: not complied is JUST FALSE, complied is NOTHING).
#ASSERT `Under form 11, am I released, given whether I have complied with the obligations marked on the release order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Variation needs the prosecutor, Dana and her sureties, if any.
#ASSERT `Under form 11, may the conditions of my release order be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor, myself and my sureties` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under form 11, may the conditions of my release order be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor, myself and my sureties` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
