§ `Cases -- A warrant for your arrest or for your committal (Forms 7, 8, 21 and 23)`

-- A warrant for Gus's arrest also authorizes entry into his flat (the box is checked). The officers knocked at 6 a.m. with reasonable grounds to believe he was in.
#ASSERT `Under form 7, may the peace officers enter my dwelling-house to arrest me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- They had only a hunch: "you may not enter ... unless you have, immediately before entering ..., reasonable grounds to believe".
#ASSERT `Under form 7, may the peace officers enter my dwelling-house to arrest me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The box is not checked on the warrant: the Form's grant of entry is not in it, so Form 7 does not cover the entry (not "no").
#ASSERT `Under form 7, may the peace officers enter my dwelling-house to arrest me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The warrant checks ground (h), the Identification of Criminals Act: the Form cites sections 512.1 and 512.2.
