-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ccc32 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc32-cases-seat.l4 -- cases for the seat layer ccc32-seat.l4: the accused's questions about the related and transitional provisions of amending Acts
-- and the amendments not in force (lines 19056-19797 of the Criminal Code text).
-- Each case states the facts a person in the seat could give; the expected value is decided by reading the provision (the layer-1 tests cover every branch;
-- these cases show the questions are wired to the rule they name, with the person's own inputs). The days are made-up days: the commencement days are not in the sources.
-- A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `1991 to 2015 -- detained, charged, sentenced or heard around a change of the law`
